window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":176,"title":"Chapter 176 A Scent She Couldn’t Shake","paragraphs":["Eira caught herself staring at Alpha Killian’s face a second longer than she should have.","The sharp line of his jaw, the steady silver-gray eyes, the way he stood close enough for his warmth to cut through the cold.","Alpha Killian noticed.","His gaze dropped to her mouth. Then he leaned in, slow enough to give her every chance to stop him.","Eira’s pulse stumbled.","For one reckless second, she thought he might kiss her.","\"I should get back inside,\" she said quickly.","She stepped away before he could close the distance. \"They’re waiting for me.\"","Alpha Killian did not try to stop her.","Eira turned and headed for the glass doors, walking faster than necessary.","--","Across town, Vincent had just picked Lainey up from the airport when his phone rang.","It was Serena. She wasn’t feeling well, she said, and didn’t have the energy to come across town. Would they mind meeting at a restaurant near her place instead?","Vincent glanced at Lainey. \"You okay with that? Serena’s not feeling great.\"","Lainey shrugged. \"Sure. I don’t care where we eat.\"","\"We’ll come to you,\" he told Serena. \"Text me the address.\"","He hung up, already looking forward to seeing her.","Lainey caught the look on his face and let out a quiet sigh.","That was one battle not worth fighting.","They got there a little early and waited out front. Serena had picked a place a few blocks from her building.","A few minutes in, Lainey’s stomach growled loud enough to make her wince.","Vincent pulled a granola bar from his coat pocket, tore it open, and handed it to her.","Lainey stared at it. \"Since when do you carry snacks around like a soccer mom?\"","\"Because I knew you’d complain about being hungry.\"","\"You really do know me.\"","\"Eat.\"","Lainey took a bite while they waited.","Vincent checked his phone. \"Serena’s probably still doing her makeup. She’s like you—she won’t leave the house until it’s perfect.\"","\"Rude.\"","A cab pulled up, and Serena stepped out with flawless makeup, a bright smile, and not a single hair out of place. She looked completely fine.","\"Vincent. Lainey. Sorry to keep you waiting.\"","She hugged them both.","\"You sure you’re feeling okay?\" Vincent asked.","\"Honestly, I’m fine.\"","They made quick small talk and headed inside, taking a booth near the back.","As soon as they sat down, Serena turned to Lainey.","\"So, are you out in California for a shoot, or just to unwind?\"","\"Just to unwind.\"","\"Too bad. My parents are back in town, so I’m stuck playing chauffeur for my parents. I probably won’t have time to show you around.\" Serena smiled at Vincent. \"You’re free, right? Keep her company.\"","\"I can take care of myself,\" Lainey said. \"Besides, your brother would kill my vibe.\"","Vincent gave his sister a look.","\"You came out here to chase him?\"","Lainey leaned back against the leather seat. \"I like him.\"","\"How many times are you gonna throw yourself at a brick wall?\"","\"As many times as it takes.\"","Serena blinked. \"You have someone you like?\"","\"Always have.\" Lainey took a sip of water. \"I’m honestly surprised my brother never mentioned it.\"","\"He’s not right for you,\" Vincent said.","\"You won’t know until I try.\" Lainey turned to Serena. \"What about you? How are things with your boyfriend?\"","Serena’s smile froze for half a second.","Her eyes flicked to Vincent, then back to Lainey.","\"Good,\" she said with a soft laugh. \"We’re good.\"","Vincent’s jaw tightened.","The server arrived with their food, saving Serena from another question.","All through dinner, Serena kept drifting off.","Whenever she thought no one was watching, a flicker of worry crossed her face. The second someone said her name, the polished smile snapped right back.","Lainey caught it every time.","After dinner, Vincent studied Serena as they stepped outside.","\"You look exhausted. Want me to run you to urgent care?\"","Serena shook her head fast, almost like the idea scared her.","\"No clinics. I just haven’t been sleeping.\"","Vincent didn’t buy it.","\"Get in. I’ll drive you home.\"","He turned to Lainey. \"Hop in the back.\"","Lainey raised an eyebrow but climbed into the back seat without arguing.","The drive to Serena’s building took barely two minutes. Vincent pulled up out front, put the car in park, and told Lainey to wait.","\"I’ll walk her up.\"","He came around, opened Serena’s door, and led her toward the entrance. Under the porch light, he stopped her.","\"You’re pregnant, aren’t you?\"","Serena’s stomach dropped.","[How does he know?","She had planned to keep it buried. Now she needed to get ahead of it before Vincent decided she was some desperate girl clinging to Sebastian for money or status.]","She let her eyes well up on cue.","\"Who told you?\"","Vincent’s gaze dropped to her stomach. He didn’t say a word.","\"Vincent, can you keep this quiet?\" Serena’s voice trembled. \"Sebastian doesn’t want the baby.\"","She lowered her head, and the tears spilled over.","Something in Vincent’s chest twisted.","\"I won’t tell a soul. Just stop crying.\"","\"Thank you.\"","She hugged him quickly, then pulled back and wiped her cheeks.","\"My parents are furious. I probably shouldn’t be seen with you for a while. Take Lainey out and show her a good time while she’s here.\"","Vincent waited until she disappeared inside, then let out a slow breath and walked back to the car.","The moment he got in, Lainey turned to face him.","\"So, Serena and the boyfriend are hitting a rough patch?\"","Vincent stared at her. \"How’d you get that?\"","Lainey rolled her eyes.","\"That sad little smile and the whole ’we’re good’ routine? Please. That’s girl code for, ’My life is falling apart, but I refuse to make it your problem.’\"","She hadn’t missed a second of Serena’s performance.","Lainey didn’t hate Serena, but she didn’t really like her either. For now, Serena was just a name and a pretty face attached to her brother’s obsession.","If Serena ever actually won Vincent over and started angling to marry into the Crawford Pack, then Lainey would pay closer attention. Until then, cheering Serena on was simply the easiest way to keep her lovesick brother from sulking.","Vincent had promised to keep the pregnancy quiet, so he left that part out.","But Serena’s love life was fair game.","To protect her image with his family, he skipped the uglier details.","\"Her boyfriend fell for another woman,\" he said.","Lainey’s eyebrows shot up.","\"Somebody actually pried a man out of her hands?\"","Serena had the kind of look that drew ambitious men like moths to a flame. Good family, a beautiful face, soft when it counted, and just enough career success to seem interesting without ever threatening a man’s ego.","\"Who?\" Lainey asked, suddenly invested.","Vincent’s expression darkened.","\"Trust me, you don’t want to know.\"","\"That bad?\"","\"This woman’s tangled up with Killian too.\"","Lainey’s expression shifted.Now she wanted the whole story."]},{"number":177,"title":"Chapter 177 A Familiar Face","paragraphs":["Lainey guessed Lila first. When Vincent’s expression didn’t so much as flicker, she moved on to Kate, then Natalie. Still nothing.","\"Okay, I give up. Just tell me already, Vince.\"","Vincent kept his eyes on the road. If this was what it took to finally kill his sister’s hopeless crush on Alpha Killian, then so be it.","\"Her name’s Eira. Alpha Killian treats her like she’s made of glass, and everyone in his circle falls right in line behind him.\"","That should paint the picture clearly enough. A man as cold-blooded as Alpha Killian Sterling was actually letting a woman under his skin.","Lainey froze for a beat.","\"How serious are we talking? Does he actually want her? And what about Serena’s guy?\" She frowned. \"Two Alphas circling the same woman? This Eira has to be way more than Serena—\"","She caught herself and bit it back. Her brother was sitting right there, and trash-talking Serena wouldn’t go over well.","But now she was hooked.","Alpha Killian had been born at the top of the food chain. He was the Alpha of one of the oldest bloodlines on the continent, a wolf whose Pack controlled territory and resources that half the packs on the coast would kill for.","For years, heiresses and wannabe Lunas had thrown themselves at him without ever earning a second glance.","And yet some woman named Eira had cracked him wide open.","Lainey had to see this woman for herself.","--","The next morning, Eira finished uploading the walkthrough shots of the place on Ashford Lane and emailed her notes over to a design studio. Nothing about the layout was structural, mostly just furnishings, so their proposal came back fast. They set up a meeting at a coffee shop downtown.","Before she left, Mrs. Jones looped a brown scarf around her neck.","\"Mrs. Jones, it’s not even that cold out yet.\"","\"The wind off the coast gets brutal this time of year. Keep it on. And drive safe.\"","\"Bye, Mrs. Jones.\" At the door, Eira crouched down to scratch both German Shepherds behind the ears. \"See you two later.\"","The designer spotted her the second she walked in.","\"Ms. Crawford, right this way. Here’s the plan. All the brands and materials are listed, so just check off whatever you like.\"","Eira scrolled through the tablet. The proposal called for an open kitchen, a balcony knocked through, and floor-to-ceiling glass.","\"Raise the balcony section into a platform so it’s set apart from the living room. Keep the same hardwood floors throughout. I don’t need much, just a dark walnut table over there and a built-in bookcase behind it in the same tone. That’s it for now.\"","\"Perfect. We’ll just need you to walk our crew through the property once they get started.\"","\"It’s Ten Ashford Lane. Everyone shows up with a photo ID, and I’ll need plate numbers and vehicle details ahead of time. It all gets logged at the gate.\"","The designer blinked. To an outsider, Ashford Lane was just a nice address in a nice neighborhood, not the kind of place that ran security like a Pack border checkpoint.","\"Got it. I’ll get out of your hair, then. We’ll keep you posted in the group chat.\"","Eira watched him go, finished her coffee, and stood up. On her way out, she bumped shoulders with a woman scrolling through her phone.","\"Sorry.\"","\"Sorry.\"","They both looked up at the same time.","The woman was polished, five-inch heels putting her at eye level with flat-shoed Eira.","Blunt bob, pearl studs.","--","Lainey barely heard her own apology. Something in the other woman’s face had snagged her, deep and insistent, and she couldn’t look away.","Eira gave a small nod and turned to go.","\"Wait.\" Lainey’s hand shot out before the word even left her mouth, closing around Eira’s wrist.","\"Can I help you?\" Eira glanced back.","Lainey barely registered the question. She was staring at those eyes, at the line of that brow. They were her father’s.","\"That one was on me back there,\" Lainey said. \"Let me buy you a coffee to make up for it.\"","\"I just had one, thanks.\" Eira slipped her wrist free and walked out.","Lainey drifted to the window, her pulse climbing.","Out on the curb, Eira slid on a pair of rimless glasses while she waited for her car. The wind off the coast swept across her profile, clean and sharp.","There it was again. Stronger this time.","That side profile was a dead match for a photo Lainey had stumbled across years ago, her father when he was young, out in the field.","A memory she’d buried a long time ago floated back up. The whispers when she was little. Funny, she doesn’t look a thing like her mom or her dad. The grown-ups always assumed a pup couldn’t follow along. She’d caught every word. Her parents had bitten the head off whoever said it, swore up and down she took after her late grandmother, and eventually the whispers died off. But the crack it left had never really healed.","Lainey touched her own cheek, her eyes locked on Eira.","She hadn’t even gotten the woman’s name.","She hurried out the door just as Eira’s car pulled up to the curb.","\"Sorry, could I grab your name? Or maybe a number? I still owe you that coffee.\"","Eira’s eyes cooled.","\"I’m good, thanks.\" She slid into the car and told the driver to go.","Following a stranger was insane, and Lainey knew it. She flagged down a cab anyway and fired off a quick text to push her afternoon plans.","The cab trailed the car clear across town, out toward the quieter streets near the water. It finally slowed at a curb where another car was already waiting. Cherry-pink, impossible to miss.","Lainey recognized it in a heartbeat. That was Lila’s car.","Lila hopped out and hooked an arm through the woman’s, and the woman who’d been ice-cold ten minutes ago actually smiled.","Lainey sat frozen in the back of the cab.","She looks like a completely different person when she smiles.","So the woman and Lila went way back. Lainey and Lila weren’t exactly close, but they’d crossed paths plenty, the kind of faces that kept turning up in the same circles.","She could hardly jump out now and start grilling Lila’s friend right in front of her. That would look bizarre, and word would only make things messier.","Then again, this actually made things easier.","If the woman was that tight with Lila, there’d be no shortage of ways to dig.","Besides, she was due at the Sterling estate that evening to see Luna Seraphina.","She’d just get the story out of Lila then."]},{"number":178,"title":"Chapter 178 One Day as His Girlfriend 1","paragraphs":["Eira had barely sat down across from Lila when her phone buzzed.","It was Alpha Killian.","[Time to make good on that favor you owe me. Come somewhere with me tonight. I need your help with something.]","Lila glanced over her shoulder, groaned, and dropped her forehead onto the table.","\"He always knows where I am. I swear.\"","\"Do you know what this is about?\" Eira asked.","\"Vincent’s sister, Lainey, is coming to the estate tonight to see my mom. You remember that whole mess between her and my brother, right?\" Lila frowned. \"He wants to use you as a human shield. The nerve of him, hiding behind a woman.\"","A favor was a favor, though, and Alpha Killian had helped her out more than once.","Eira texted back.[Where are you? I’ll come to you.]","[Stay put. I’ll come get you.]","Half an hour later, he found her at a coffee shop downtown. His sister was sitting right beside her.","\"You’re everywhere,\" he said bluntly.","Lila bit down on her straw. \"You’re the one who keeps showing up.\"","Eira got straight to the point. \"What do you need me to do tonight?\"","Alpha Killian’s silver eyes settled on her.","\"We’re going to the family estate. I need you to help me handle Lainey.\"","\"As what?\"","\"My girlfriend.\"","Lila nearly choked on her straw.[Whoa. Since when did he grow a backbone?]","Eira studied his face, looking for some hidden motive, but she found nothing.","\"How long?\"","\"Forever!\" Lila blurted out. Then she covered her mouth. \"Did I actually say that out loud?\"","Alpha Killian shot her a look cold enough to frost the windows.","\"One day,\" he told Eira.","\"All right, Mr. Sterling.\"","\"You’re still calling me ’Mr. Sterling’?\"The corner of his mouth lifted slightly. \"Better get used to things being different now.\"","Lila’s eyes lit up.","\"So she has to call you by your first name now. Or maybe ’babe.’ Or ’sweetheart.’\"","Eira turned to her with a blank expression.","\"Sweetheart, eat your food.\"","Lila wrapped both arms around Eira’s arm and rubbed her nose against Eira’s shoulder. Then she gave her brother a smug look.","Alpha Killian pinched the bridge of his nose. The air around him seemed to drop several degrees. Lila quickly sat up straight.","\"Okay, okay. Eira, just try it. Killian is fine. He won’t bite. Probably.\"","\"Lila.\" He did not even blink. \"Have I ever laid a hand on you?\"","\"No, sir!\"","Eira held back a laugh.","\"I’ll use your name.\" She paused for a moment. \"Killian.\"","She said it clearly and without rushing.","A low \"Mm\" rumbled in his chest.","When no one was looking, the corner of his mouth curved up.","He checked his watch. It was 5:12 p.m.","\"Let’s go.\"","When Eira stood, his gaze fell on the pale line of her neck. Her scarf quickly covered it, and he looked away.","The estate stood deep inside Sterling territory. Beyond the outer gate, the night patrol moved along the borders, guarding them as tightly as the oldest Packs always had. Floodlights shone over the fences.","A security checkpoint stood at the entrance to the drive. The distant sounds of the Pack carried through the darkness.","The Sterlings had protected this land for generations. Nothing that did not belong there was allowed to cross the border.","By the time they turned onto the long driveway, night had fully fallen.","Eira’s phone buzzed again.","[Eira, were you the one who introduced me to Dr. Shaw? Could you help me with one more thing?]","She blocked the number before she finished reading the message.","\"Sebastian again?\" Lila asked, watching Eira’s thumb move across the screen.","\"Mm-hmm.\"","\"What does he want now? Is he still groveling, feeding you a bunch of lies, and begging you to come back while he plays house with Serena Winthrop?\" Lila rolled her eyes. \"You can see right through his little act.\"","\"It’s about Dr. Shaw,\" Eira said. \"He signed his patents over to another company, not Hale.\"","Lila’s face lit up. \"Seriously? That’s the best news I’ve heard all week. We’re celebrating tonight. Eat whatever you want. Our chef is amazing.\"","Alpha Killian’s mouth twitched. \"Sounds like a plan.\"","\"Without Dr. Shaw’s patents, Sebastian has nothing valuable enough to keep Hale Group afloat. He’s done.\"","\"What if he finds something else?\" Lila asked.","\"Keep dreaming.\"","\"Not a chance. The universe isn’t about to let that man catch a break.\"","Alpha Killian turned to Eira and lowered his voice. \"He’ll be even more desperate to find you now. Watch your back.\"","\"Finn is already waiting for him to slip up,\" Alpha Killian continued. \"One wrong move, and Alpha Carter hears about it. One serious mistake, and Finn takes his seat on the board.\"","Eira thought about Alpha Sebastian’s message and frowned. \"Chasing me won’t help him. Dr. Shaw already signed the patents over to another company. Even if he hadn’t, I’d never go back and beg the old man for Sebastian.\"","Alpha Killian raised an eyebrow. A faint look of satisfaction crossed his face.","The car pulled to a stop. The driver opened the door, and Lila hopped out first.","\"No rush,\" she called over her shoulder. \"I’ll go give Mom and Dad a heads-up.\"","Alpha Killian offered Eira his arm.","She hesitated. Alpha Sebastian had never once done that in public. In that small but important way, Alpha Killian was the complete opposite of him.","When she still did not move, Alpha Killian raised an eyebrow.","\"Well?\"","Eira placed her hand on his forearm. Solid muscle, firm and steady beneath her palm.","\"Let’s go, Killian.\"","He started toward the house, his long strides quickly leaving her behind.","\"Eira. Do you know how to ask for what you need?\"","The question caught her off guard. \"Yes.\"","\"Then ask me to slow down.\"","His voice was cold, but she did not feel threatened. He sounded like he was teaching her a lesson.","\"Killian, slow down.\"","\"Use your words. Always.\"","He shortened his stride at once and matched his pace to hers."]},{"number":179,"title":"Chapter 179 One Day as His Girlfriend 2","paragraphs":["By the time they entered the house with their arms linked, Luna Seraphina and Lila were waiting with matching, knowing smiles.","The staff kept their heads down, though they still sneaked glances at the couple. No one wanted to make Eira uncomfortable. If they did, the young Alpha might stay single for the rest of his life.","Alpha Julian was the only one who looked completely unfazed. He was sprawled across the sofa.","\"You’re back.\"","\"Alpha Julian. Luna Seraphina.\" Eira dipped her head.","Alpha Julian stood and smiled. \"Welcome home.\"","\"Thank you.\"","\"No, thank you,\" Alpha Julian said. \"You’re taking this menace off my hands. He’s all yours now. No returns.\"","He nodded toward Alpha Killian.","Lila burst out laughing. Eira tried to hold it in, but a smile tugged at her lips. She glanced at Alpha Killian.","\"Go ahead and laugh,\" he said. \"I can take it.\"","His family teased him freely, but no one questioned his authority as Alpha.","Luna Seraphina reached for Eira’s hand and led her to the sofa.","\"Have some fruit. Take whatever you like. Dinner won’t be ready for a little while. We’re still waiting for a guest.\"","\"Thank you, Luna Seraphina.\"","Eira relaxed as soon as she sat beside her. A small smile appeared before she could stop it.","Alpha Julian pulled Alpha Killian a few steps away from the others. Once they were out of earshot, he lowered his voice.","\"Lila says you only convinced Eira to be your girlfriend for one day.\"","\"Don’t start.\"","Alpha Julian gave him an amused look. Alpha Killian clearly wanted more than one day.","If Eira had offered to stay longer, he would have asked her. Pushing for even one extra day, however, would probably have made her walk away from the whole arrangement.","Alpha Julian’s expression said he knew exactly what his son was thinking.","Before he could say anything else, the butler entered.","\"Alpha Julian, the guest has arrived.\"","Lainey swept into the room with two arms full of gift bags.","\"Seraphina. Julian. Lila. Killian.\" She greeted everyone with a bright smile before setting the bags down.","Eira stood and froze.","It was the woman she had bumped into at the coffee shop earlier that day.","Lainey’s smile faltered when she saw Eira. What was this woman doing here, in the Sterling home?","\"Seraphina,\" Lainey said, quickly recovering, \"who’s your guest?\"","Alpha Killian moved to Eira’s side.","\"This is my girlfriend, Eira. Eira, this is Lainey, Vincent’s sister. Her family has had ties to my mother’s Pack for years.\"","Eira gave Lainey a small nod. So the woman from the coffee shop was Vincent’s sister. She never would have guessed. The siblings looked nothing alike.","Lainey’s gaze shifted to Alpha Killian. He stood beside Eira with easy familiarity, as if he belonged there. Lainey’s smile tightened.","Eira returned her greeting with a polite smile.","Lainey looked Eira over from head to toe.","[So this was the woman Vincent kept talking about? The woman who had stolen Serena Winthrop’s man? The woman the most untouchable Alpha in the region had just called his girlfriend?]","Alpha Killian caught the unfriendly look in Lainey’s eyes and stepped in front of Eira, blocking her view.","\"Get a good look?\"","Lainey looked away. \"I was just surprised.\"","She had to admit it. Eira was beautiful, but not in a way that demanded attention. Her beauty was quiet and understated. Calm eyes, delicate features, and an expression that gave almost nothing away.","Everyone in the region had expected Alpha Killian to fall for someone loud, fiery, and impossible to ignore. Instead, he had chosen someone as reserved as he was.","And from this angle, Eira did not really look like Lainey’s father. The resemblance only appeared from one particular angle.","Lainey felt relieved, but she still could not decide whether she was disappointed.","Luna Seraphina stepped in before the silence turned awkward.","\"Lainey, you must be starving. Come on. Dinner’s ready.\"","\"Sounds perfect.\"","Lainey reached automatically for Luna Seraphina’s arm, just as she did whenever she visited. But Luna Seraphina had already turned toward Eira.","\"Eira, come sit with us.\"","Before Eira could move, Alpha Killian gently caught her by the wrist and guided her toward the dining table.","Luna Seraphina blinked.\"Is he seriously protecting her from me? I’m his mother.\"","Lila suddenly burst out laughing.\"Mom, that’s nothing. He gets annoyed whenever I stand too close to Eira. He’s been working all day to ruin my reputation with her.\"","For a second, Eira wondered if Alpha Killian’s behavior meant something more.","Then she remembered they were only pretending to be together. He was simply making the act convincing.","\"Lila,\" Alpha Killian warned.","\"What? I can’t even stand next to Eira without you giving me that look.\"","Luna Seraphina shook her head.","\"Lila, take Lainey to the table. We had the kitchen prepare all her favorite dishes.\"","Lila linked arms with Lainey and led her toward the dining room.","Alpha Killian pulled out a chair for Eira. It was his usual seat.","\"Sit here.\"","Eira glanced at him, then sat down.","The staff began bringing out the food.","Three dishes caught Eira’s attention right away. They were all comfort foods she had grown up eating at the orphanage.","Her eyes lit up before she could stop them. She started to look toward Lila, but Alpha Killian gently lifted her chin with two fingers and turned her face back toward him.","\"I picked those,\" he said. \"I told the kitchen exactly what to make.\"","Eira’s eyes widened. \"How did you know?\"","\"You looked at the plates, then looked at Lila. It wasn’t hard to figure out.\"","\"Thank you,\" she said softly. \"Killian.\"","\"Mm.\"","Lila nearly melted into her chair.\"How did you even know what she liked?\"","\"Pay attention to someone long enough, and you learn.\"","Alpha Killian said it so naturally that Eira almost believed they had been together for years. Lainey seemed to believe it too.","They did not need to hold hands or steal kisses. The way Alpha Killian looked at Eira said enough.","Once Alpha Killian fell quiet, dinner settled into a warm and comfortable rhythm.","Lainey raised her glass toward Eira.","\"I owe you an apology for earlier. I’m a photographer. When I saw you at the coffee shop, I thought you’d look great in front of a camera. I wanted your name and a way to reach you.\"","Eira waited.","Lainey tilted her head. \"Especially your eyes. They say a lot. You look like you’ve got a whole story behind them.\"","So that was what the coffee shop had been about.","Eira lifted her glass but shook her head. \"I’m sorry, but I don’t like having my picture taken.\"","\"No problem. If you ever change your mind, you know where to find me.\"","Lainey let it go without pushing.","Eira understood what Kate had meant. Lainey knew how to read a room. She knew when to back off, and she never made anyone feel trapped.","Even so, something about the way Lainey looked at her felt strange. Eira just could not put her finger on it."]},{"number":180,"title":"Chapter 180 Keeping Her Distance","paragraphs":["After dinner, Luna Seraphina walked Lainey to the door and arranged for the driver to take her home.","\"You look exhausted,\" Luna Seraphina told her. \"Get some rest. You need to take care of yourself.\"","Before she left, Lainey quietly slipped a business card into Eira’s hand.","Eira accepted it to keep things from getting awkward.","Once the door closed behind Lainey, Eira turned to Luna Seraphina.","\"Is Lainey okay?\"","Luna Seraphina’s expression softened.","\"She was born with a heart condition. It isn’t serious as long as she keeps a regular schedule and avoids too much stress.\"","--","A few miles from the Sterling estate, Lainey opened her text thread with Serena and typed:","[I ran into a woman at the Sterling estate. Eira. She’s a real operator.]","The word was enough to make Serena call.","Lainey answered, but cut her off before she could start asking questions. \"It’s late. I need to get some sleep. We’ll talk in person.\"","She ended the call and slipped her phone into her purse.","--","Back at the Sterling estate, Lila put on her most innocent expression.","\"Killian, why’d you suddenly go quiet?\"","Alpha Killian was stretched out on the sofa, looking relaxed and perfectly at home. His half-lidded eyes slid toward Eira.","Everyone else followed his gaze.","Eira had stood in front of rooms full of reporters without blinking, but being watched by the Sterling family somehow made her feel more exposed.","She met Alpha Killian’s eyes. \"You can talk now.\"","\"If nobody pointed me out, you’d forget I was here.\"","Eira stared at him for a moment. \"Actually, you can keep quiet.\"","Lila burst out laughing. Her laughter echoed through the house.","The evening wore on. Outside, members of the Sterling Pack made their rounds along the perimeter, checking the gates and scanning the tree line. The patrols had guarded the territory for generations, keeping the estate and everyone inside it safe through the night.","Inside, the mood stayed warm and easy.","When Eira yawned, Alpha Killian stood immediately.","\"Dad, Mom, we’re heading out.\"","Then he turned to Lila. \"You stay here.\"","\"Fine.\" Lila slumped back against the sofa. She had not even asked to go with them to Number Nine.","Eira reached over and lightly messed up her hair as she walked past. \"Good night, Lila.\"","\"Night!\" Lila called, waving with a grin.","Alpha Killian guided Eira toward the door before his sister could start teasing her again.","As they left, Eira let herself sink into the warmth of the evening. She had never experienced anything quite like it.","Her mentor had been too busy when he was alive for her to spend much time at the Thorne estate. After he died, she began visiting his widow. That house had been warm in its own way, but the Sterling estate felt different. It was louder, closer, and full of the easy affection of people who had grown up together.","Alpha Julian rarely spoke, but he always seemed to know what Luna Seraphina needed before she said a word.","Luna Seraphina was gentle and graceful, with a playful streak that Lila had clearly inherited. Lila and Alpha Killian argued constantly, but their teasing never turned truly cruel.","And then there was Alpha Killian.","Eira glanced at him as they walked. He was looking at something on his phone, but the moment he noticed her watching him, he looked up.","\"Hmm?\"","He lowered the phone.","Eira shook her head. \"Nothing.\"","\"Barry says the clinic came up with a whole line of herbal wellness drinks,\" Alpha Killian said. \"He wants you to be the first one to try them.\"","Eira raised an eyebrow. \"Did Dr. Wood actually say that?\"","\"See for yourself.\"","Alpha Killian held the phone out to her, but kept it just far enough away that she had to lean closer to read the screen.","Eira leaned in to read the screen. Her hair slipped over her shoulder, the soft ends brushing Alpha Killian’s jaw before trailing across his neck.","A clean, warm scent followed.","Alpha Killian’s breath caught.","\"Dr. Wood never said anything about turning me into a lab rat,\" Eira said, settling back once she’d finished reading. \"He just wanted you to ask whether I’d be willing to try it.\"","She glanced up—and found him already looking at her.","Not past her. Not out the window. At her.","\"What?\" she asked.","\"Nothing.\"","He looked away first, took off his coat, and draped it across his lap.","\"The air-conditioning’s too high.\"","Eira glanced at the vents. If anything, the car was warm. But he’d been drinking, and the faint color along his jaw could have been the wine.","\"Is it?\" she said.","\"You’re not cold?\" His voice had dropped, quieter than before.","\"No.\"","\"Then leave it.\"","The words came out low and clipped, and for a moment neither of them moved. The space between them had shrunk somewhere along the way, close enough that she could feel the heat coming off him.","Eira held still. So did he.","She didn’t know what she was waiting for. Neither, it seemed, did he.","Then Alpha Killian exhaled and turned back toward the window, breaking whatever had just tightened in the air.","Eira looked down at her phone, her pulse a beat too fast, and told herself it was the wine on his breath, the closeness, the late hour. Anything but him.","Alpha Killian cleared his throat.\"So. You coming tomorrow?\"","\"I have work.\"","\"You run a team of several hundred people. They’ll survive one day without you.\"","Before she could argue, he sent Barry a voice message.","\"She’s coming.\"","Barry replied almost immediately. Alpha Killian ran the message through text first, making sure Barry had not decided to argue with him, then handed the phone to Eira.","\"Perfect timing,\" Barry said. \"Grandma was just asking about you.\"","Eira thought of Mrs. Wood. She had never properly thanked the older woman. This was a good chance.","\"Sure.\" She paused, then asked, almost as an afterthought, \"Are you going too, Mr. Sterling?\"","They had been away from the estate for less than ten minutes, and she was already putting distance between them again."]},{"number":181,"title":"Chapter 181 The Herbal Tea","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian gave her a cool look.","\"Eira. How many hours are there in a day?\"","\"Twenty-four.\"","\"Good. You can count. Ask me again.\"","She frowned at him, then played along.","\"Are you going to the Wood clinic tomorrow, Killian?\"","\"No.\"","\"Okay, then.\"","That shut him up.","After a beat, he added, \"Tomorrow’s packed. I’ve got a board meeting, then a cross-border council call.\"","Eira knew. She had been shadowing him as his assistant for nearly a month. The first day of the month was always brutal: back-to-back meetings, reports that never seemed to end, and calls with neighboring Packs about shared border patrols and energy rights.","Not wanting her stuck at the clinic by herself, Alpha Killian said, \"You could bring Lila.\"","\"Lila’s buried too. It’s December, and graduation’s right around the corner.\" Eira smiled. \"What does she like? I want to get her something.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression darkened.","\"No idea.\"","Eira blinked. There it was again—that sudden prickliness. The man changed moods faster than Seattle weather.","When they reached Number Nine, Alpha Killian spoke before she could open the door.","\"I’ll pick you up from the clinic when I’m done.\"","\"Don’t bother.\" Eira held up her phone. \"I’ll call a car.\"","His eyes held hers for a beat too long.","Then he pressed the button, and the privacy screen slid up between them.","Alpha Killian watched her walk toward the door, then let his head fall back against the seat.","She could run a division, dismantle a rival’s numbers in an afternoon, and stare down a boardroom full of Alphas twice her age.","But put him this close, and she still hadn’t figured out the simplest thing in the car.","Clueless. Completely, maddeningly clueless.","--","The next morning, Mrs. Jones fussed over Eira for a bit and then sent her on her way.","\"Cold snap’s coming in. Grab a scarf and gloves, both of them. I put some hand cream in your bag.\" She pushed a black umbrella into Eira’s hands. \"This time of year, it snows out of nowhere around here.\"","Eira didn’t recognize the umbrella. \"Where’d this come from?\"","\"It’s Alpha Killian’s. He’s got a whole fleet of cars, and they’re all stocked. Trust me, he’s not gonna miss one umbrella.\" She saw Eira hesitate and added, \"Really, Miss Crawford, it’s fine.\"","If anything, he’d be glad she took it.","On the way over, Eira stopped at a shop and picked up a soft cashmere scarf for Mrs. Wood. With older folks, something thoughtful and useful always went further than something flashy.","The clinic smelled like dried herbs, with a hint of something warmer underneath. The second she walked in, Barry spun around.","\"Eira, over here!\" He glanced past her. \"You came by yourself? Alpha Killian didn’t come with you?\"","\"He’s slammed today.\"","Barry’s face fell. He’d set this whole visit up himself. His staff had put together a special couples’ tea, and he’d wanted the two of them to name it together. So much for that idea.","\"Would it be okay if I saw Mrs. Wood first?\" Eira asked.","He waved her toward the back garden. She’d been there before and knew the way.","The moment she turned the corner, Barry grabbed his phone and texted Fiona.","[Clinic’s got a new drink. Come try it.]","[Pass.]","[Might make you glow and knock you right out.]","[On my way.]","He smirked.[ Rolling out the red carpet.]","When he looked up, Eira was walking his grandmother out. A soft new scarf was wrapped around Mrs. Wood’s neck. The old woman was beaming.","Mrs. Wood patted the scarf. \"See that? Girls actually pay attention. Unlike certain grandsons I could name.\"","She shot him a look sharp enough to curdle milk. \"Come on, Eira. Let’s go try whatever they cooked up back there. But hang on—we make Barry drink first. If he lives, we’ll try it.\"","Eira held back a laugh. \"Deal.\"","They sat down at the old wooden table, which was covered with nuts and dried fruit.","\"Help yourselves,\" Barry said. \"We’ve got one more person coming.\"","--","Half an hour later, Fiona walked in, boots and all. She scanned the room, spotted Barry first, then Eira.","They’d only met once, on that yacht.","\"Miss Crawford. Didn’t expect to see you here.\"","\"Ms. Carter.\"","Fiona sat down, took the warm towel Barry handed her, and wiped her hands.","\"So where’s this miracle tea?\"","Mrs. Wood raised her brows. \"Miracle? Barry, what have you been telling people?\"","\"It’s not a scam,\" he said quickly. \"The benefits are real. I just can’t put it in an ad, or the FTC’ll come down on me.\"","Fiona ignored him. Her eyes drifted back to Eira. Even sitting there quietly, Eira drew the eye. No wonder Alpha Sebastian had married her.","Eira noticed the look. There was no scorn in it, just curiosity. \"Was there something you wanted to ask me, Ms. Carter?\"","The staff brought out four cups, all warm and sweet-smelling.","Fiona didn’t even glance at her cup. \"So are you and Sebastian actually getting divorced?\"","To outsiders, the whole thing was a black box. Plenty of gossip, no real facts. Fiona had figured they were already done.","Serena was carrying his kid, so what was left to hang onto? But breaking a Mate bond took two people. If Alpha Sebastian dug in his heels, then with the required cooling-off period on top of it, Eira could be tied up in court for a long time.","Barry frowned. \"You still not over the guy, Fiona?\"","Eira looked up, a little surprised. She had a thing for Sebastian?","She’d just opened her mouth to say the divorce was already finalized when Fiona snapped back at Barry.","\"Don’t be dense. I’m asking because it matters. Whether she leaves Sebastian doesn’t just affect him. It affects the whole Carter portfolio.\"","Of all the companies the Carters had money in, Alpha Sebastian’s pulled in the most.","Barry let out a quiet breath.","Fiona turned to Eira. \"Sebastian’s been at the office all weekend. This morning they called him into Carter headquarters to answer some questions. Everybody wants to know if he can keep this marriage of yours from falling apart.\""]},{"number":182,"title":"Chapter 182 A New Rival","paragraphs":["\"What difference does it make if he saves the marriage or not?\" Eira asked.","Fiona’s smile turned sharp. \"A big one. Trust me.\"","Eira was no ordinary Omega. Her judgment and connections did not just support Alpha Sebastian. They kept his entire tech division running.","If Alpha Sebastian saved the marriage, the Carters could keep the affair quiet. If he failed, his reputation would take a hit inside his own company and across the Carter group.","One bad move could send him from the top of the ladder straight to the bottom.","Fiona did not care if Alpha Sebastian went down on his own. But if the news reached the Carters too late, they would have no time to prepare for the damage. That mattered even more now that her father was trying to move her into the brand division.","Alpha Sebastian’s scandal would become a Carter scandal.","She did not explain all of that.","She did not need to.Eira had spent enough nights listening to Alpha Killian break down Pack politics to understand how one problem could spread through an entire organization.","\"Sebastian and I are already divorced,\" Eira said.","Fiona’s eyes widened. \"Divorced? He actually signed the papers?\"","It was hard to believe. Alpha Sebastian would have held on to Eira even before he knew who she really was. He had needed her to keep the Hale household running.","After learning her true identity, he would have had even more reasons to keep her close.","A woman who could support both his family and his business was not someone he would have let walk away easily.","Eira had never been more grateful that she had finished the divorce before her identity came to light. Otherwise, she could have ended up trapped in a nightmare of legal and family problems.","\"Your drink is getting cold,\" Mrs. Wood said, cutting into the conversation.","She patted Eira’s hand. \"Do not waste time looking back, sweetheart. What is gone is gone.\"","Eira smiled. \"I know, Mrs. Wood.\"","\"Good girl.\"","Fiona was still trying to process it. Alpha Sebastian had agreed to the divorce and kept it quiet?","She wanted to call her father at once, but she still was not sure what divorced meant under Pack law. Breaking a Mate bond required a mandatory one-month cooling-off period.","If the final registration was not completed, the bond might still remain legally active.","She opened her mouth to ask another question, but Barry cut her off.","\"Fiona, I invited you here to try the new blends.\"","Then he leaned closer and lowered his voice.","\"Alpha Killian knows Eira is here. If you upset her, he won’t just come after me. He’ll come after you too.\"","Fiona swallowed the rest of her questions.","Alpha Killian did not believe in playing nice. Almost nobody wanted to find out what happened when they ended up on his bad side.","\"Fine. I’ll try the drinks.\"","She took two sips, pulled out her phone, and took a picture of the tasting tray.","\"I’m sending this to a friend,\" she said.","She was actually sending it to her brother.","[Get down here. Your dream girl is at the Wood clinic.]","Fiona’s phone buzzed.","Barry: [Why are you calling the Carter kid here?]","Fiona: [To chase the dream girl, obviously.]","Barry: [Alpha Killian likes her. You didn’t notice that on the yacht?]","Fiona: [So what? May the best wolf win. Finn might beat him to it. He’s younger, has more free time, and probably has better stamina.]","Barry stared at the message.","He took a screenshot, half tempted to send it straight to Alpha Killian and half afraid Alpha Killian would set Fiona on fire.","In the end, he sent Alpha Killian a safer message.","[Alpha. Finn Carter is on his way to the clinic. He’s interested in Eira.]","That was as far as Barry’s loyalty went.","Alpha Killian was stuck in a board meeting and never saw the message.","Finn had already finished the last report Alpha Sebastian had left him and headed straight for the clinic.","He walked in with a shy smile.","\"This is my brother, Finn,\" Fiona said. \"He was nearby, so he figured he’d wait here and drive home with me.\"","Finn looked at Eira. His eyes were bright and eager, but he kept his manners under control.","\"Good to see you again, Eira.\"","They had met once before on the yacht.","Eira gave him a polite nod. \"Mr. Carter.\"","\"You call everyone else by their first name. Just Finn.\"","Finn took the seat beside Eira.When she reached for the next cup, he picked it up first.\"Let me get that.\"","Eira remained calm around him. She did not seem affected by his attention.","The tea was another story.","She pulled out her phone and showed Barry the notes she had typed.","\"These are my thoughts on each blend. Flavor, aftertaste, and how long the calming effect lasts. I also added notes about which formula might work best for post-patrol recovery.\"","Barry read the screen with interest.\"Is this a science thing?\"","\"Don’t ask me,\" Fiona said. \"I don’t do labs.\"","Barry took a picture of Eira’s notes and sent it to Alpha Killian.","[Alpha, I invited her to a tasting and she gave us a full report. If you two ever argue, is she going to hit you with a presentation?]","Alpha Killian finally checked his phone when the message came through.","He could not decide whether to thank Barry for saying YOU TWO or strangle him for mentioning an argument.","Then he saw the message underneath.","[Finn was at the clinic.]","His expression went flat.","He looked at Kate. \"What’s left on my schedule?\"","\"The cross-border council call.\"","\"Push it to nine tonight. Clear everything else.\"","Kate blinked. \"Tonight?\"","\"Yes.\"","Alpha Killian stood and walked out."]},{"number":183,"title":"Chapter 183 He Saw Her","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, Alpha Sebastian made it through the Carter executives’ grilling.","The Snowmark project gave him enough cover that no one pushed too hard on Dr. Shaw’s patents. When Alpha Carter brought it up, Alpha Sebastian kept his face calm.","\"Dr. Shaw’s buried right now. I’ll get the details from him later.\"","He did not take a full breath until he stepped outside the tower.","On the drive back, he switched to a spare SIM card and pulled up Eira’s number. He was about to text her when Jordan called.","\"We found Sam.\"","Alpha Sebastian straightened. \"Where?\"","Jordan sent him a photo.","Alpha Sebastian opened it.","Sam was fifteen now. Taller, but still unmistakable. His clothes hung loose on his thin frame, faded and frayed at the seams. The cold had cracked his cheeks raw.","He looked worse than he had at the shelter.","In the picture, he was kicking a ball down an alley with a group of younger kids.","\"That’s him.\" Alpha Sebastian’s brow tightened. \"What happened? Why isn’t he in school? Where’s his coat?\"","\"He’s living with a cousin’s family. Six people in a two-bedroom rental. The other three kids are enrolled in school. Sam isn’t.\"","\"Why?\"","\"They told the school they were homeschooling him because of his autism. But the district has no enrollment record, no homeschool paperwork, no lesson records, and no IEP. He hasn’t received any formal education or special services.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression hardened.","\"Autism doesn’t mean he can’t learn.\"","\"I know.\" Jordan’s voice dropped. \"There’s more. The family applied for SSI shortly after they took him in. They were approved, and the payments have been going into an account managed by one of the adults in the household.\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","\"According to the application, they claimed they provided full-time care and educated him at home. So far, we haven’t found any proof of either. I’m checking the payment records now.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","At the shelter, Sam had barely spoken to anyone. He would not answer questions or join the other children. He only stayed close to Eira.","The year his relatives came to take him home, Sam had spoken for the first time.","He had looked at Eira and called her Sister.","Eira wrote her number on a slip of paper and placed it in his hand.","\"Keep it somewhere safe.\"","She had him repeat the number back to her twice, correcting him whenever he missed a digit.","\"And if you ever feel sad, call me. Okay?\"","Sam had stayed with her as a quiet worry.","The following year, she had tried to ask about him, but the shelter could not release his records without legal paperwork, a request from a verified relative, or an attorney.","After that, the trail went cold.","\"What do you want me to do?\" Jordan asked.","\"Go to him. Use Eira’s name. He’ll talk to you.\"","A few minutes later, Jordan started a video call.","Sam’s face filled the screen. Hope flickered in his eyes, then faded when he saw Alpha Sebastian instead of Eira.","\"Sam, do you remember me?\" Alpha Sebastian asked. \"I’m Eira’s husband. I was with her when you left the shelter.\"","Sam stared at him.","The silence stretched.","Then he gave a small nod.","\"Eira changed her number,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"I’ll give you the new one. You can call her whenever you want.\"","He glanced at Jordan. Jordan nodded.","\"Do you want to go to school, Sam?\"","Sam’s eyes lit up.","Alpha Sebastian softened his voice. \"Go with Jordan. He’ll take care of everything.\"","Sam glanced at the man beside him. Jordan gave him an encouraging nod.","\"Hold on, Jordan,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","Sam stepped out of the frame. A moment later, Jordan’s face appeared on the screen.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression hardened again.","\"Find him a school with a strong special education program. Small classes. Trained staff. A safe campus. Have the district arrange an evaluation and get an IEP in place.\"","\"Got it.\"","\"Get him out of that house. If the family refuses, involve Child Protective Services and our attorney. Report the SSI issue to the Social Security Administration and request a review of the representative payee.\"","Jordan looked up. \"And the money?\"","\"Do not touch the account. Do not give the family a chance to move it. Let the attorney and the SSA handle the hold.\"","\"Understood.\"","\"Get him a real winter coat. Warm boots. Whatever else he needs. Once counsel clears the placement, bring him to me.\"","By the time Alpha Sebastian reached the office, Finn was gone. The front desk said he had left early.","Alpha Sebastian sighed and pulled up Finn’s number. Before he could call, a new post appeared in his feed.","A location tag.","A tasting tray.","Several cups on a table, with four hands visible in the frame.","Alpha Sebastian tapped the post.","It was a short video.","A woman’s voice called a name.","He played it again.","\"Eira.\"","Fiona’s voice.","Alpha Sebastian checked the location.","Eira was at the Wood Clinic with Fiona and Finn."]},{"number":184,"title":"Chapter 184 One Word and He Folds","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian walked into the Wood family clinic at exactly two in the afternoon.","The back room was warm and crowded. A stockpot simmered on a portable burner near the open door, sending steam toward the ceiling. The room smelled like chicken broth, rosemary, and something sweet baking in the kitchen.","Through the haze, Alpha Killian spotted Eira.","Her sea-gold hair was twisted up with a tortoiseshell claw clip. She was carrying a basket filled with fresh herbs, bread rolls, and small jars of honey, looking for somewhere to put it down on the old farmhouse table.","Alpha Killian’s pulse hit hard.","Eira looked up as if she could feel his stare through the steam.","Their eyes met.","\"Barry,\" she said quietly. \"Alpha Killian’s here.\"","Barry turned.","Alpha Killian stood in the doorway.First came the long legs. Then the black shirt, the broad shoulders, and the face that made half the city forget what they had been saying.","His silver-gray eyes locked on Eira.Then they moved to Finn , sitting beside her.","The warmth disappeared from Alpha Killian’s gaze.His wolf had spotted another male inside his territory.","Finn felt the pressure hit him before Alpha Killian said a word. It pushed against his chest, heavy and cold. His wolf lowered its head on instinct.","Finn kept his face still. Just barely.","\"Finn.\" Alpha Killian’s voice was quiet.\"Move.\"","One word.It sounded polite if you did not know him.","Barry knew better. Alpha Killian was giving Finn a chance to move before he stopped asking.","Finn’s fingers tightened around his spoon.He almost stood.","Then he remembered that Eira was single now.She was fair game.","And he had been sitting there first.","\"There’s an empty seat by the window,\" Finn said. He nodded toward the wooden bench across the table. \"That one’s yours.\"","The room went quiet.","The old rule was simple. Whoever arrived last took the open seat.","But Alpha Killian had never cared much for other people’s rules. Not many people in the city had the nerve to remind him of one.","Fiona had spent years talking trash about Alpha Killian behind his back. She had even encouraged Finn to go after Eira.","Face-to-face, though, she would not have dared say a word.","She shot Barry a look, silently telling him to do something.","Barry pretended not to notice.","The silence stretched.","Eira finally set the basket on the table and stood.She crossed to the window bench, picked up the bowl in front of her, and moved it aside. Then she nodded to the seat beside her.","\"You can sit here, Alpha Killian.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression went flat.","Finn felt the weight of those silver eyes settle on him again.","For one second, he thought Alpha Killian might ignore Eira and make him move anyway.","Then Alpha Killian turned and sat down beside her.","Close enough that their shoulders almost touched.","He leaned back against the wall and looked at her.\"Alpha Killian?\"","Eira pressed her lips together. Right. She kept forgetting.","\"Would you like some rosemary chicken soup?\" she asked.","She pushed her untouched bowl toward him.","Then, after the briefest pause, she added, \"Killian.\"","The cold around him disappeared.","Alpha Killian picked up the spoon, tasted the broth, and nodded once.\"Not bad.\"","Barry’s gaze darted between Alpha Killian and Eira. That’s it? One bowl of soup and this man was placated?","Across the table, Fiona’s jaw dropped.This was the same Alpha who could make grown wolves apologize for breathing too loudly?","Finn’s expression fell.","\"Everybody get some broth in you before we add the meat and greens,\" Mrs. Wood called from beside the stockpot. \"Once everything’s in, it won’t taste half as good.\"","\"You’re just sitting down to eat now?\" Alpha Killian asked.","Eira reached for the ladle, but Alpha Killian got there first. He took her bowl and spoon, filled the bowl, then glanced at her as if waiting for an explanation.","\"The broth’s been simmering for over two hours,\" she said. \"Mrs. Wood says it helps keep you warm through the winter. Good for your energy, too.\"","[Good for your energy?Then Eira should be having more of it.]","Alpha Killian filled her bowl to the brim, then served himself.","Once everyone started eating, Finn slipped right back into charming golden-boy mode.","\"What are you in the mood for?\" he asked Eira. \"I can make it for you.\"","Before she could answer, Alpha Killian cut in.","\"Aren’t you supposed to be learning the ropes at Hale Group, Finn? Seems a little early to be skipping out for lunch.\"","\"You’re here too, Alpha Killian.\"","\"I took over the Sterling Pack and the company when I was twenty.\"","Alpha Killian took another spoonful of broth.","\"You’re twenty-three and still in training.\"","Finn froze.","It was just a fact.So why did it land like a punch to the ribs?","Fiona jumped in before he could respond.","\"Finn joining the company at twenty-three is still pretty impressive.\"","\"Compared to you?\" Alpha Killian said. \"Sure.\"","Fiona’s mouth snapped shut.","Barry dragged a hand down his face.","Every single one of them was lining up to take a swing at the Alpha.","They could learn something from Eira and keep their mouths shut long enough to eat.","Eira, at least, was doing exactly that.","Ever since Mrs. Jones had started cooking those herbal dishes back at the estate, Eira had developed a serious weakness for them.","The winter lamb stew was especially good. The heat had already reached the soles of her feet, and a few more bites sent warmth spreading through her chest and limbs.","She looked up and caught Alpha Killian watching her.\"Aren’t you going to eat?\"","\"I am.\" His gaze dropped to her bowl. \"What do you want?\"","It was the exact same question Finn had asked her.","Eira could have reached across the table and served herself. But Alpha Killian, stubborn as ever, clearly wanted her to tell him what she wanted.","She gave him a puzzled look, then named three of the greens spread across the table.\"Dandelion greens. Chickweed. And nettles.\"","Alpha Killian stared at her.He had never heard of any of them.","Finn spotted his opening.He looked over the food. Mushrooms and baby cabbage—those he recognized. But dandelion greens? Chickweed? Nettles?","His hand stopped halfway to the serving bowl.","Alpha Killian noticed.\"Tch.\"","Finn slowly lowered his hand.","Alpha Killian turned back to Eira.\"Eat the meat.\"","It was lamb stew. Meat was practically the whole point.","But Eira had already had enough. She wanted the greens.","Every one of those plants had been used as an old Pack remedy. She had grown up eating them at the Omega home, long before she knew they were supposed to taste medicinal.","Barry watched the two men eyeing one another across the table.Then he cleared his throat and gave a pointed glance toward the bowl of greens.","Alpha Killian and Finn reached for it at the same time.Each grabbed one side of the serving bowl.","Finn refused to let go.","Alpha Killian never let go of anything he wanted. Nobody took something out of his hands.","The tension snapped tight.","Then a pair of wooden serving tongs slid between them, scooped up a generous handful of greens, and dropped them straight into Eira’s bowl.","Everyone looked over.","Eira had taken the tongs herself.She calmly added another handful to her bowl.","\"Problem solved,\" she said."]},{"number":185,"title":"Chapter 185 We’re Already Divorced","paragraphs":["Barry nearly bit through his cheek trying not to laugh.","Two grown Alphas were locked in a silent standoff over a bowl of greens. The woman they were fighting over had already served herself and gone back to eating as if nothing had happened. Fiona couldn’t even look at them anymore.","Eira stirred the wild greens into the hot broth, took a bite, and paused.","It needed a little heat.","She glanced toward the kitchen.","\"You want something spicy?\" Alpha Killian asked. His deep voice rumbled close to her ear.","Eira looked up, surprised that he had been paying attention.","\"If they have any,\" she said.","Alpha Killian turned toward Barry.","\"Does the clinic have hot sauce?\"","\"Not that I know of.\"","\"Then get some.\"","Barry opened his mouth to explain that he was a doctor, not a short-order cook. One look from Alpha Killian shut him down.","\"Right. I’m on it.\"","He pulled out his phone and searched for the nearest grocery store. Frank’s RedHot, Tabasco, and Cholula were all available. He ordered the fastest option, then added a small container of crushed red pepper flakes in case Eira wanted more heat.","He paid extra for rush delivery and texted the driver to hurry.","Barry had barely placed the order when the front door opened again.","The delivery driver was not the first person to arrive.","An unwelcome guest was.","Alpha Sebastian stepped out of his car and looked up at the Wood family clinic.","This was his second visit. The place looked bigger than he remembered. Heavy wooden beams framed the building, and floor to ceiling windows let warm light spill onto the sidewalk.","He walked inside, told the receptionist he was looking for someone, and headed straight toward the back.","\"Alpha Sebastian.\" Barry stepped in front of him. \"Patients stay in the front area. The back is private.\"","Alpha Sebastian knew Barry worked for Alpha Killian. But this was Sterling territory, so he kept his voice calm.","\"I’m here for Eira.\"","\"And don’t waste your breath telling me she isn’t here. I saw Finn’s post.\"","Barry’s eyes widened.[Great. The kid’s picture had given everything away.]","\"No invitation, no entry,\" Barry said. He raised his phone. \"Try to force your way back there, and I’m calling the police.\"","Alpha Sebastian ignored him.","He had to see Eira.","If he could not see her here, he might not get another chance anywhere else. Southridge Estates had two guards and two dogs. The moment he got close, those dogs started howling.","The Silix Institute and Sterling Group were just as hard to get into. They might as well have been locked vaults.","When Alpha Sebastian tried to follow Eira, federal security intercepted him.","Even keeping an eye on Lila had led nowhere. She went to school, went home, and sometimes visited the old family estate. That was it.","If he missed Eira today, when would he get another chance?","Dr. Shaw’s project could not wait. Neither could Carter Group. That morning, Alpha Carter had hauled Alpha Sebastian into his office and given him one clear order: close the deal before the annual council meeting.","He was not asking for a miracle. He just wanted Alpha Sebastian to bring back something instead of showing up empty-handed.","Alpha Sebastian was more desperate than anyone realized. He had already rehearsed what he would say. He would apologize, cut Serena off for good, and make sure his family never went near Eira again.","She would forgive him. Their feelings would come back. His career would get back on track.","Then he stepped into the back room and stopped cold.","Eira and Alpha Killian sat close together on the bench by the window, their shoulders nearly touching in the warm light.","Alpha Killian turned toward her.","A moment later, Eira looked up at him.","From where Alpha Sebastian stood, they looked far too comfortable together.","Heat rushed behind his eyes. His wolf snarled beneath his skin.","\"Eira!\"","The entire table fell silent.","Barry came in right behind him.\"I tried to stop him.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened as he glared at Eira and Alpha Killian sitting shoulder to shoulder.","Finn frowned. \"What are you doing here?\"","Fiona glanced at her watch. \"It’s not even three. Shouldn’t you be at the office?\"","She had once thought soft-spoken Alpha Sebastian was a much better man than cold, sharp-tongued Alpha Killian. Turns out, she had backed the wrong wolf.","Alpha Sebastian barely acknowledged either of them. He walked around the table and reached for Eira’s arm.","She pulled away before he could touch her.","His hand closed around nothing.","Alpha Killian looked up at him. His voice was calm, flat, and cold.","\"And what exactly does Alpha Sebastian think he’s doing?\"","Alpha Sebastian was the one standing over them, but the moment those silver-gray eyes locked onto his, a chill ran down his spine.","\"Alpha Killian, this is between Eira and me. It’s a family matter.\"","\"A family matter?\" Eira’s brow furrowed. \"What family could we possibly have left?\"","\"Eira.\" Alpha Sebastian’s control started to crack. \"I know you’re angry. Whatever this is, we can talk about it at home.\"","Mrs. Wood’s expression hardened.","\"Alpha Sebastian, is it?\" she said. \"The first time you barged into my clinic, you didn’t ask how Eira was doing. You went straight to blaming her. Now you’re back, trying to pull her out of here like she’s supposed to jump whenever you snap your fingers. What makes you think she belongs to you?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face tightened.","She was right. Both times, he had lost his temper.","\"Sebastian.\"Eira’s voice cut through the room.Your parents still haven’t told you, have they?\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","\"That we’re already divorced.\""]},{"number":186,"title":"Chapter 186 The Divorce He Never Knew About。","paragraphs":["The word divorced had been following Alpha Sebastian for weeks.","His parents had mentioned it first. Isabella had thrown it around like an insult. Serena had hinted at it. Ethan had said it outright. Even Vincent , who was neither friend nor ally, had used it against him.","Alpha Sebastian had refused to take any of them seriously. A mate bond could not be dissolved without his signature, and he would never sign away Eira.","But hearing the word from Eira herself felt like an invisible fist closing around his heart.","\"Eira, we are not getting divorced.\" His voice cracked. \"You matter to me. To my reputation. To the Carter deal. We can fix this.\"","Eira stared at him as if he were being deliberately stupid.","\"I said we’re already divorced. The day I left Sterling Group, the dissolution certificate came through.\"","\"Certificate?\" Alpha Sebastian’s face went pale. \"What certificate?\"","He reached for her shoulder.","Alpha Killian moved first.He wrapped one arm around Eira and pulled her back beside him. His body settled between her and Alpha Sebastian, broad shoulders squared, silver-gray eyes turning colder than a winter wind across the northern territories.","His wolf had made its choice.","Protect. Guard. Claim.","Alpha Sebastian’s wolf snarled, wild with jealousy.","Barry quickly guided his grandmother toward the front room, then hurried back. There was no way he was missing the rest of this disaster.","\"If you don’t believe me, call your parents,\" Eira said. \"You signed the papers yourself. Your father used his Pack Council connections to rush the dissolution through. You know how many officials he has in his pocket.\"","\"No.\" Alpha Sebastian shook his head, but panic flashed across his face. \"I never signed anything. I would never sign away my mate. How could I?\"","\"You did.\"","Eira’s voice stayed calm, which somehow made it worse.","\"It wasn’t a property transfer. It was part of the dissolution agreement. Did you really think I wanted that condo after you and Serena used it as your private getaway?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s pupils tightened.His heart stumbled.","She knew.","She actually knew.","\"I...\" His voice failed him.","\"Save the whole ’nothing happened with Serena’ speech,\" Eira said. \"It only worked on you. That was when she got pregnant, wasn’t it?\"","Her gaze dropped briefly to his face.","\"You two left enough evidence behind. You didn’t even bother changing the sheets.\"","Fiona made a strangled sound somewhere between a curse and a gag.","He had brought his mistress into the home he shared with Eira and slept with her in their bed. What was next? Was the CEO of Hale Group too cheap to get a hotel room?","She looked at her brother.","Her sweet, easygoing little brother had turned into a walking thunderstorm.","Alpha Killian remembered Eira spending hours sick to her stomach at Sterling Group. His jaw tightened.","The broth still steamed on the table, but the air around him had turned ice-cold.","Alpha Sebastian’s panic collapsed into terror.","She knew everything.","\"No,\" he rasped. His eyes were rimmed red. \"I never signed anything. We’re not divorced. The certificate never reached me. That’s not possible.\"","So his parents really hadn’t told him.","Eira frowned.","The Hales had wanted her gone more than anyone. She had agreed to keep the divorce quiet until the bidding ended only because she was afraid Alpha Roger would drag his feet.","Every day the paperwork stayed unfinished meant more lawyers, more Pack Council hearings, and more time tied to a bond that meant nothing to her anymore.","She had a future to build. Alpha Sebastian was no longer her mate, and he had no right to keep tearing her life apart.","That was why she had blocked his texts. Every message started with Let me explain. She had stopped reading after those first three words.","She had assumed his sudden desperation meant he knew their marriage was over. Why else would he keep chasing her?","But that was not it.","He had come crawling back because the gossip had shredded his reputation, and he needed his Luna to clean up the mess.","He wanted her to protect his name, his position, and the millions that came with it.","What was there left to say?","\"Sebastian.\" Eira’s voice was flat and calm. \"Whether you believe it or not, we’re done.\"","That calm destroyed him.","If she had screamed, he could have fought back. If she had hated him, he could have begged for forgiveness. But there was no anger in her voice. No hurt. No love.","Nothing.","He remembered how she used to look at him. She was distant with everyone else, but never with him. She could sit in his office for hours while he worked late, quiet and patient, never asking him to stop.","Four years of that.","Then she had walked away, dissolved their bond, and looked at him like he was a stranger.","How had he lost her so completely?","\"You’re lying, right?\" His voice shook. \"Serena means nothing to me. You’re the one I want. You.\"","Alpha Killian gave a low, humorless laugh.","\"That’s what you call wanting her?\" His silver-gray eyes turned cold. \"You gave Eira the bare minimum and told her it was love. You gave Serena everything, then stood here and swore there was nothing between you.\"","Alpha Sebastian flinched.","Alpha Killian leaned back against the bench, one arm still braced behind Eira.","\"Own it. Say you loved Serena, and I might almost respect you.\" His mouth curved without warmth. \"But you won’t. You don’t have the guts.\"","Alpha Sebastian jerked as if Alpha Killian had struck him. Whatever control he had left finally snapped.","\"Alpha Killian, what gives you the right to stand beside her?\""]},{"number":187,"title":"Chapter 187 My Girlfriend","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian’s hand slid around Eira’s waist and pulled her firmly against his side. His silver-gray eyes locked on Alpha Sebastian, cold and openly challenging.","\"Eira’s my girlfriend now.\"","The words hit the room like a gunshot.","The Carter siblings stared at him.Since when?","Barry nearly choked. He had stood at Alpha Killian’s side for years, and the Alpha had never breathed a word about Eira. But the announcement was classic Alpha Killian. He never told people what he planned to do. He simply informed them after it was done and expected everyone else to catch up.","Barry took the news in stride.","Alpha Sebastian looked like he had been hit.","His face darkened. Red flashed across his eyes as his wolf slammed against his control.","\"That’s not possible.\" His voice came out raw. \"You can’t be with her.\"","He stared at Eira as if she were the only person in the room who could undo Alpha Killian’s claim.","How could she be Alpha Killian’s mate? How could she sit there and let another Alpha touch her?","Eira barely seemed to hear him.","Her gaze had dropped to Alpha Killian’s arm around her waist. He had held her like this once before, at Sterling Estates. Now he was doing it again in front of everyone.","His body heat seeped through her coat. His hand rested over her waist, warm and steady, as if he had every right to keep her exactly where she was.","His fingers tapped lightly against her side.","Eira looked up.","Alpha Killian glanced toward Alpha Sebastian, then back at her.","[Eyes forward, sweetheart. He’s falling apart, and you’re staring at me.]","Eira had a rare talent for pushing a wolf to the edge without raising her voice or lifting a finger.","Alpha Sebastian watched the exchange, his breathing turning rougher by the second.","His eyes pleaded with her.","Tell him this isn’t real.","Eira gave him a small, calm nod.","\"Yeah. That’s right.\"","For now, at least, their twenty-four-hour girlfriend story was still holding together.","Something inside Alpha Sebastian split.","His hands curled into fists. His nails dug into his palms, but he barely felt it. His wolf wanted out. It wanted Alpha Killian’s throat, consequences be damned.","If the room had been empty, Alpha Sebastian would have attacked him.","Instead, he stood there and watched Alpha Killian keep Eira tucked against his side as if she belonged there.","Eira did not spare Alpha Sebastian’s pain a second glance.","\"If you came here hoping I could help with Dr. Shaw’s patent, you might as well save yourself the trouble and leave,\" she said. \"He already licensed it to another company. The deal is done.\"","The news hit the room like a wrecking ball.","Finn’s eyes widened.\"Dr. Shaw already signed it away?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jealousy twisted into panic.","He had thought he still had room to negotiate. He had thought he could fix the deal, win back Eira, and keep Hale Pack from falling further behind.","Now the Carter siblings had heard everything.","Alpha Carter would know within the hour.","His chance to move Hale Pack up the Council rankings had gone up in smoke.","Fine.","Let the deal go.","Let the Council hear about it.","Right now, he cared about only one thing.\"Eira, about the dissolution...\"","\"You want to argue over whether it’s legal?\" she cut in.","Her voice remained calm. Not angry. Not hurt. Not even bitter.","That calm hurt more than shouting ever could.","\"Ask your parents,\" she continued. \"Your father has your Mate Bond Dissolution Certificate.\"","Alpha Killian’s arm tightened around her waist.","It was a small movement, but Alpha Sebastian saw it.","A warning.","A claim.","Eira was not standing alone anymore, and Alpha Killian wanted everyone in the room to understand that.","Alpha Killian gave Barry a brief glance.","Barry stepped forward with a polite smile that held no warmth.","\"Alpha Sebastian, you’re not welcome here. You can walk out on your own, or I can have two of my people walk you out. You’ve already made enough of a scene. Don’t make this worse for yourself.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked past Barry to Eira.","She did not look back.","Her attention stayed on the hand at her waist, on the Alpha standing between her and the man who had once called himself her mate.","That final rejection broke whatever restraint Alpha Sebastian had left.","His eyes burned red.","\"You’re really choosing him?\" he asked.","Eira finally looked at him.\"This was never about choosing between you and him. I chose myself.\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","Alpha Killian’s mouth curved faintly, but there was no humor in his eyes.\"You heard her.\"","The words were soft.","The threat beneath them was not.","Alpha Sebastian gave Eira one last desperate look, searching for even a trace of the woman who had once waited for him, cooked for him, and defended him.","He found nothing.","He turned and walked out.","The Carter siblings followed, both of them too stunned to care about lunch anymore.","A moment later, Barry’s phone buzzed. The grocery delivery had arrived.","He returned with a paper bag filled with hot sauce and crushed red pepper flakes.","\"Got the stuff you wanted, Alpha.\" Barry lifted the bag. \"You still eating?\"","Eira looked at the hot sauce and laughed softly.\"Absolutely.\"","\"Good.\" Alpha Killian’s mouth curved.","His hand stayed at her waist as he guided her back to the table."]},{"number":188,"title":"Chapter 188 It Was Him","paragraphs":["Across town, Isabella was tearing through drawers in the Hale family study.","Eira had told her to find Serena’s ultrasound picture. Isabella had started with Alpha Sebastian’s apartment, but the locks had been changed. She’d cracked the new keypad code on her second try. Alpha Sebastian had never been good with passwords.","The apartment had been almost empty. Alpha Sebastian had already packed up most of his things, so she’d found nothing there except bare shelves and half-filled boxes.","That was why she’d moved on to the family study.","Now, as she searched the desk, something caught her eye. The bottom drawer didn’t sit quite right.","She pried it open and found a hidden compartment beneath it.","Inside were two folders.","A Registered Mate Bond Certificate.","And a Mate Bond Dissolution Certificate.","Both carried the names Alpha Sebastian Hale and Eira Crawford.","\"My brother dissolved his bond with Eira?\" Isabella blurted.","The study door swung open.","Luna Margaret took one look at the papers and snatched them from Isabella’s hands.","\"Stop digging through things that don’t concern you.\"","\"When did this happen?\" Isabella demanded. \"Why didn’t anyone tell me?\"","\"You’re a child. What would you even understand?\" Luna Margaret shoved the folders against her chest and pointed toward the door. \"Get out. And don’t say a word to your brother. Are we clear?\"","Isabella stepped into the hallway.","Alpha Roger was coming in from the foyer, still wearing his wool overcoat and leather gloves.","Isabella looked from him to Luna Margaret. \"Mom found the dissolution papers.\"","Luna Margaret lowered her voice. \"She found them.\"","Alpha Roger’s face tightened.","Luna Margaret poured him two fingers of bourbon from the decanter on the bar. Her hand shook with anger and regret.","\"Who could’ve guessed Eira had that kind of backing? She gave Alpha Sebastian exactly what he wanted, then convinced us to rush the final registration through the Council. We thought we were getting rid of her.\"","She handed him the glass.","\"All that talent, and she kept it hidden. If she’d given us even one clue, just one, none of this would’ve happened.\"","The keypad chimed.","Only one person besides the household staff had the code.","Luna Margaret immediately stopped talking.","Alpha Roger shot Isabella a warning look.","The door opened.","Alpha Sebastian walked in.","He ignored their forced smiles and crossed the room with his tie loosened, his coat hanging open. He looked less like a corporate executive than a man who had run out of places to hide.","\"The dissolution papers.\" His voice was low. \"Did you two arrange this?\"","Luna Margaret’s stomach dropped, but she forced a smile.","\"Who’s been filling your head with nonsense?\"","\"Eira.\"","Alpha Roger frowned. \"She promised she’d keep it private.\"","Alpha Sebastian let out a hollow laugh.","\"So it was you.\"","Neither of them answered.","\"Why?\" His voice rose. \"Why do you always interfere with my life? With my bond?\"","\"Sebastian.\" Alpha Roger set down his bourbon and straightened. \"If you hadn’t looked down on Eira from the start, we never would have gotten involved.\"","Isabella pressed herself against the wall.","\"She’s right,\" she said quietly. \"You ran Eira into the ground too. We only treated her that way because we watched you do it first.\"","Serena’s voice echoed through Alpha Sebastian’s mind.","The person who hurt Eira wasn’t me. The person you should blame is you.","His hands began to shake.","For four years, he had watched his family treat Eira like she was beneath them and said nothing.","He had let them push her out, then signed the dissolution agreement without giving it a second thought.","He had been wrong from the beginning.","But the certificate was real.","Eira had said his parents were holding it.","Alpha Sebastian’s red-rimmed eyes fixed on his father.","\"Where is it?\"","Luna Margaret and Alpha Roger exchanged a look.","Alpha Roger gave her a short nod.","She disappeared into the study and returned with two leather folders. One held the Registered Mate Bond Certificate. The other held the Mate Bond Dissolution Certificate.","She handed them to Alpha Sebastian.She handed them to Alpha Sebastian.","He stared at the folders.","Twice, his father had dismissed them as Council paperwork. Twice, Alpha Sebastian had chosen not to ask questions.","His fingers tightened around the leather.\"Quite the operator, Dad.\"","Alpha Roger lowered his gaze.\"I had no idea Eira was a federal researcher.\"","\"That’s not the point!\"Alpha Sebastian’s voice cracked through the room, a growl buried beneath it.Alpha Sebastian’s voice cracked through the room, a growl buried beneath it.","\"You had no right to dissolve my bond behind my back.\"","Isabella flinched. She had seen Alpha Sebastian angry before, but never like this. He had never raised his voice at Alpha Roger, the one person in the house no one dared challenge.Isabella flinched.","She had seen Alpha Sebastian angry before, but never like this. He had never raised his voice at Alpha Roger, the one person in the house no one dared challenge.","Alpha Roger’s expression hardened.","\"If Eira hadn’t turned out to be a federal researcher, give me one reason she belonged in this pack.\""]},{"number":189,"title":"Chapter 189 The Certificate in His Hands","paragraphs":["\"She was my mate.\" Alpha Sebastian’s chest rose and fell hard. \"I chose her. That made her my Luna and part of this family. If you wanted her gone, you should have come to me. I would have kept her away from the pack myself. You don’t run her out like some rogue crossing the border.\"","\"And what exactly would changing that now accomplish?\" Alpha Roger’s voice softened. He was not willing to destroy what was left of his relationship with his son. \"Your mother and I regret how things played out. We tried to fix it. But it’s done. What happens next is on you.\"","Luna Margaret rushed to smooth things over.","\"Sweetheart, Eira was the one who filed. She put the papers right in front of you and got you to sign them. This isn’t your father’s fault, and it isn’t ours. We only wanted what was best for you.\"","She stepped closer.","\"Back then, we didn’t know what Serena was really like. We thought cutting Eira loose and marrying Serena would help you. Her family had money, connections, and influence. We thought all of that would finally work in your favor. We never meant to hurt you.\"","She reached for his arm.","Alpha Sebastian pulled away.Not roughly. Just firmly enough to make his answer clear.","The room went quiet.","Isabella’s expression softened.","\"Bro, if you really want her, then go get her back. You won her once. Why can’t you do it again?\"","She leaned closer, lowering her voice.\"And this time, the whole family will treat her right. I promise.\"","Luna Margaret nodded along.","Eira had always been useful. She had managed the household, handled pack events, and taken care of everyone. Luna Margaret had once thought she was too plain to show off.","Now Eira had credentials, recognition, and a powerful name behind her. She would turn heads at every Council gathering.","\"Isabella’s right,\" Alpha Roger said. \"You won her once. You can win her back. The bond was dissolved today. You could re-bond tomorrow.\"","His words carried an ugly assumption.","Eira had no family of her own. No influential bloodline. No powerful relatives to protect her. Everything she built could still become part of the Hale family.","Alpha Sebastian was the only one who understood how rotten it was.","He was the only one who knew how badly he had hurt her.","If Eira hated him, that would at least mean she still felt something. Anger could last longer than love. Hate could still keep two people tied together.","But the way she had looked at him was worse.","She had been calm. Completely calm. She had handed him the truth about their divorce as casually as if she were checking the weather.","She had looked at him with less emotion than she had shown the first day they met.","At least back then, there had been a spark.","Alpha Sebastian clutched both folders and walked out without another word.","His family could only watch him leave.","Luna Margaret let out a heavy sigh.","\"He’s really done this time.\"","Alpha Roger frowned.","What was left to do? The relationship had been dead for a long time.","\"Maybe we should talk to Eira,\" Luna Margaret said slowly. \"Put in a good word for him.\"","Isabella nodded.","Alpha Roger shot them both a warning look.","\"If you two show up, all she’ll remember is every miserable day she spent in this house. If you run into her, be polite. Be kind. That’s all.\"","\"Obviously,\" Luna Margaret said.","Isabella’s eyes shifted as she thought it through.","\"So, based on the way he’s acting, he wants Eira back. He doesn’t want Serena, right?\"","Alpha Roger’s expression darkened.","\"What about Serena’s baby?\"","Luna Margaret thought back to the tense meeting with the Winthrops.","\"Your brother is leaning toward ending the pregnancy. He’s afraid that if the baby is born, Eira will dig into their finances. If she finds out he’s been using marital money to support Serena, he could be in serious trouble.\"","\"And Serena? Is she keeping it?\"","\"She says she needs time to think,\" Luna Margaret replied. \"She’s probably afraid Eira will come after her for the money.\"","\"No wonder she disappeared. She won’t answer calls or texts.\" Isabella’s mind raced. \"If she keeps the baby, there’ll be an ultrasound appointment. If she doesn’t, she’ll have to go to a clinic. Either way, she’ll have to show her face somewhere.\"","--","Across town, Fiona and Finn stepped into the Carter estate and flagged down the housekeeper.","\"Where’s Dad?\"","\"In the sitting room. Vincent Crawford is visiting.\"","Fiona frowned.","A few minutes later, Alpha Carter came out with Vincent. Vincent gave the siblings a polite nod before heading for the door.","\"Dad, why was Vincent here?\" Fiona asked.","\"Just a social call,\" Alpha Carter said. \"His sister will be in town for a while. You’re starting with the brand division soon, so use Lainey for the campaign shoot.\"","So Vincent had been trying to find work for his sister.","Fiona almost laughed.","Lainey Crawford needed jobs? People usually had to fight to book her.","Finn barely heard them.","Two things were burning through his mind.","\"Dad, Alpha Sebastian and Eira are divorced.\"He paused, then added, \"And Shaw licensed his patent to another company.\""]},{"number":190,"title":"Chapter 190 Take Me Back","paragraphs":["The Wood family clinic still smelled of simmering broth, mint, and fresh herbs.","Eira had spent nearly an hour picking through the lamb stew, eating mostly the vegetables until she was too full to take another bite.","\"Have some broth, sweetheart,\" Mrs. Wood said. \"It’ll settle your stomach.\"","\"It’s gone lukewarm,\" Barry muttered, peering into the stockpot. \"It was still steaming when we sat down.\"","Eira reached for the ladle.","Alpha Killian got there first.","He slid his untouched bowl in front of her and kept one broad hand around the rim. The veins stood out across the back of it.","\"Have mine. It’s still hot. I haven’t touched it.\"","His voice was low beside her ear, warm enough to brush across her skin.","Something flickered in Eira’s eyes.","\"Thanks.\"","\"Mm.\"","By the time they finished eating, it was after four. Dinner was no longer happening.","Alpha Killian still needed to stop by Sterling Tower, so he took Eira with him.","The moment they stepped into the lobby, Eira headed toward the R&D wing.","Alpha Killian turned his head and gave her a cool, warning look.","[Try it.]","Eira stopped.","He nodded toward the private elevator.","\"Fifty minutes until five fifty-two.\"","She looked at him. \"Five fifty-two?\"","\"A full day means a full day. Not one minute less.\"","Right.","The twenty-four-hour girlfriend deal.","She still owed him fifty minutes. For now, she was technically his girlfriend, and apparently that meant going upstairs with him instead of disappearing into the lab.","But what was she supposed to do up there? Keep him company while he worked? Sit in his office and wait for him to finish?","Before she could ask, Alpha Killian placed a light hand at the small of her back and guided her toward the elevator.","The doors closed behind them.","\"Do girlfriends usually tag along to their boyfriends’ offices?\" she asked.","The question was out before she realized how ridiculous it sounded.","Alpha Killian glanced down at her.","\"Sometimes.\"","\"Sometimes?\"","\"Boyfriends do it too.\" His mouth twitched. \"They also wait around while their girlfriends finish their work.\"","Then his expression grew more serious.","\"Eira, forget how Alpha Sebastian treated you. He never learned how to treat anyone properly. And forget whatever the Hales taught you to accept as normal. There was nothing normal about that family.\"","Something tightened in her chest.","She had known very few families up close. There had been her mentor and his wife, the Davies household, and a few brief glimpses of what a healthy family looked like.","The Hales were the only family she had ever lived with long enough to understand.","Now that she was away from them, Alpha Killian’s family was the only other one she knew.","Compared with the Sterlings, the Hales looked even more broken.","\"Understood,\" she said.","And she meant it.","The corner of Alpha Killian’s mouth lifted.","\"Good.\"","The elevator carried them toward his office and the fifty minutes she still owed him.","When the doors opened, the familiar executive floor came into view.","Eira’s old desk was still in its usual spot. Her things had not been packed away or moved. Her notebooks were stacked beside the monitor, and the small mug she used sat exactly where she had left it.","Natalie and Kate brightened when they saw her.","They were already starting to wave her over when they noticed Alpha Killian beside her, standing there like a stone-faced security detail.","Their hands stopped halfway up.","Eira walked over to them by herself.","\"Go on, Killian. I’ll wait out here.\"","Kate and Natalie exchanged a long, loaded look.","Alpha Killian gave them both a brief glance, then turned toward his office.","He had work to catch up on.","Eira took her old seat, opened the company laptop, and got back to work.","Through the glass wall of his office, Alpha Killian could see her whenever he looked up.","Five fifty-two came and went.","Neither of them mentioned it.","Eira was too busy working on the company laptop.","Kate glanced at her screen, saw the equations, and immediately looked away. She had a liberal arts degree. That was way beyond her.","With a nine o’clock overseas call on his schedule, Alpha Killian sent his driver to take Eira home.","Natalie and Kate stayed late for overtime.","Eira saved her files, waved good night, and texted him.","[Heading out. Good night, Killian.]","His reply came almost at once.","[Mrs. Jones set dinner aside for you.]","A small smile tugged at Eira’s lips. That unfamiliar warmth stayed with her all the way home.","It vanished the moment she stepped out of the car.","Alpha Sebastian stood at the gate.","His perfectly styled hair was a mess. His dress shirt was wrinkled, his tie hung loose, and his suit pants were torn at the legs. Clear bite marks showed through the fabric.","Two German shepherds strained against their handlers, snarling with their lips pulled back from their teeth.","Security told Eira Alpha Sebastian had been there since seven. One of the dogs had already bitten his calf, but he still refused to leave.","His bloodshot eyes lit up when he saw her.\"Eira—\"","The dogs lunged between them.","Alpha Sebastian froze.","\"Miss Crawford!\" Mrs. Jones hurried out of the house in her apron, still holding a spatula. \"Come inside, honey. Dinner’s ready.\"","Eira did not look at Alpha Sebastian.","\"Coming, Mrs. Jones.\"","\"Eira!\"","He lunged after her.","One of the dogs snapped onto his calf as the handlers grabbed his arms. Alpha Sebastian fought through the pain, reached past them, and caught Eira by the wrist.","\"I didn’t do it,\" he said through clenched teeth. \"I never signed the papers. I never even got the certificate. It doesn’t count. None of it counts. I tore it up!\"","Eira turned and looked at him.","He was bleeding, disheveled, and barely holding himself together.","She felt nothing.","\"So you tore it up,\" she said. \"The dissolution is already registered with the Pack Council. Your approval isn’t required.\"","Her voice stayed calm.","\"Sebastian, we’re done.\"","\"No.\" He shook his head. \"I was wrong, Eira. I never should’ve let Serena back into our lives. I never should’ve let my family treat you like that. Give me one more chance.\"","He pulled his wallet from his pocket and shoved several cards toward her.","\"These are yours. Debit, credit, access to my accounts, my investments, my shares. Everything.\"","He fumbled with his phone and opened his banking app.","\"I bought you a Porsche. It was supposed to be a gift. I just never found the right time to give it to you.\"","He held out the key fob.","Eira stepped back.","\"Keep it. The dissolution papers were the best gift you ever gave me.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared at her, refusing to accept the answer.","When the money, the car, and his promises failed to move her, he raised his hand. His bond ring still sat on his finger.","\"Eira.\" His voice dropped to a pleading whisper. \"I’m not taking this off. We can re-bond. We can fix this.\"","He took one careful step toward her.\"Please.\"","Eira looked at the ring, then at him.\"Go home, Sebastian.\"","The handlers pulled the dog off his leg.","For once, Alpha Sebastian did not fight them.","He only stood there, staring at Eira as if she had just sentenced him to a life he could not survive."]},{"number":191,"title":"Chapter 191 You Lost Me","paragraphs":["Eira held his gaze, her voice calm and final.","\"I’d rather die than ever bond with you again.\"","The words hit Alpha Sebastian like a punch to the chest.","\"Eira... why?\"","She almost laughed.","\"You cheated on me, and you’re still asking why? Are you hearing yourself?\"","\"Just forgive me. Give me one more chance. I swear I’ll never—\"","\"There won’t be a next time.\"","She signaled for the guards to release him. With a soft click of her tongue, the two German shepherds trotted to her side and crouched at her heels, hackles raised.","Mrs. Jones stepped behind Eira, still wearing her apron and gripping a spatula like a weapon. The guards flanked them, watching Alpha Sebastian closely.","Alpha Sebastian rubbed at his bleeding calf.","\"You keep acting like this was one mistake,\" Eira said. \"One apology, one dramatic promise, and everything goes back to normal.\"","\"I know I hurt you.\"","\"No. You know you’re losing me. That’s not the same thing.\"","His face tightened.","\"I made mistakes, Eira. But I never stopped caring about you.\"","\"You cared when it was convenient.\"","\"That isn’t fair.\"","\"Fair?\" Eira’s eyebrows lifted. \"Fair would have been telling me the truth before you brought Serena back into our home. Fair would have been defending me when your family treated me like hired help. Fair would have been giving me the loyalty you gave her.\"","Alpha Sebastian shook his head.","\"I was confused. I thought I could fix everything.\"","\"You thought you could keep both of us.\"","His mouth opened, but no answer came.","Eira gave him a cold smile.","\"Don’t look surprised. That’s exactly what you did.\"","\"I can make it right.\"","\"No, you can’t.\"","\"I’ll cut Serena off. I’ll make my family apologize. I’ll give you whatever you want.\"","\"I don’t want anything from you.\"","\"Everyone wants something.\"","\"I don’t.\"","His expression cracked.","Desperate, he reached for the only language he understood.","\"I can give you your own company. A house. A new car. You’ll never have to work for anyone again.\"","Eira stared at him.","\"There it is.\"","\"What?\"","\"You still think this is a negotiation.\"","His face went pale.","\"I’m trying to show you that you matter to me.\"","\"No. You’re showing me what you think I’m worth. Money, a title, a house, and a few shares if you’re feeling generous.\"","\"That’s not what I mean.\"","\"It’s all you know how to offer.\"","His hands began to shake.","\"I don’t care about Dr. Shaw’s patent anymore,\" he said. \"It’s gone. Fine. I don’t care about the company or the Council. I only care about you.\"","\"You always say that after you lose something.\"","His face twisted.","\"Did you forget that I stood beside you at your mentor’s funeral? I drove you back to the Omega home. I stayed with you through every rejection letter after graduation.\"","He was reaching for the woman she had been.","The woman who had loved him.","Eira let out a short, bitter laugh.","\"So that’s your whole case? A funeral, a ride home, and a few rejection letters?\"","Alpha Sebastian fell silent.","\"You showed up when I was at my lowest, and I mistook that for love. I was drowning, and you were the first hand I could reach.\"","Her voice stayed steady.","\"So I held on. I gave you everything. I thought I was finally getting a real family and a real home.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes reddened.","\"I loved you.\"","\"You loved what I did for you.\"","\"That’s not true.\"","\"I cooked your meals while you funded Serena’s career. I handled your family’s errands while you flew across the country for her birthday.\"","\"I didn’t know how much I was hurting you.\"","\"You knew enough to hide it.\"","That stopped him.","Eira continued.","\"We were newly bonded, and you were sending Serena love letters. You bought her an expensive designer bag, then handed me the cheap freebie that came with it.\"","Alpha Sebastian flinched.","\"You wanted her to be the glamorous career woman. You wanted me to quit my job, stay home, and raise your pups.\"","His lips parted.","\"You bought her diamonds. You signed me up for a fertility class.\"","\"I thought you wanted a family.\"","\"I wanted a real one. A home where people actually cared about each other.\"","Eira’s voice stayed calm, but her eyes were ice-cold.","\"I always wanted a pup. One healthy pup, raised in a loving home. You shut that conversation down every year. Then, out of nowhere, you decided you wanted an heir and acted like giving me one was some generous offer.\"","She gave a short, humorless laugh.\"That was when I knew I was done.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face went pale.","\"I was going to sit down with you and end things like adults. I was going to let you go to Serena. But you wouldn’t sign. Everyone in the Pack told you to finalize the dissolution, and you refused every time.\"","Her gaze hardened.","\"You weren’t protecting our bond. You were keeping me trapped in a relationship that had already died.\"","\"No,\" he rasped. \"The gifts I gave Serena were compensation. I knew I could never bond with her. I never planned to dissolve ours. I couldn’t stand losing you, Eira.\"","Eira stared at him.","\"You couldn’t stand losing control of me.\"","Alpha Sebastian flinched.","\"Was that what our bond was to you? Something you could keep locked away while you pursued someone else?\"","She shook her head.","\"You had the title. The money. The house. The final say in everything. I had to keep shrinking myself just to fit into the life you wanted.\"","Her voice remained steady.","\"That wasn’t a partnership, Sebastian. It was a power imbalance with a mate bond attached.\"","\"I’ll change,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"I swear I will.\"","Eira did not even blink.","Mrs. Jones had been wiping her eyes during the argument. Now she stepped forward, angry enough to forget she was still holding a spatula.","\"Alpha Sebastian, did you ever bother to notice how exhausted she was?\" she demanded. \"She was skipping meals, working herself into the ground, and trying to manage a household that treated her like staff. You called that love?\"","Her voice rose.","\"She has a dishwasher now. She has help. She has people who actually notice when she hasn’t eaten.\"","Eira reached back and gently caught Mrs. Jones by the arm.","\"Mrs. Jones, please stay behind the dogs. He’s bleeding, and we don’t know whether he’s current on his rabies shot.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression fell.","For one brief second, he had thought Eira was worried about him.","She was worried about Mrs. Jones.","\"Don’t come back here,\" Eira said. \"And stop making this worse for yourself.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared at her.","\"If you truly believe you were wrong, write it down. A full confession. Put in writing that you betrayed our bond for Serena.\"","Eira never expected him to do it.","\"I’ll write it,\" Alpha Sebastian said immediately.","Her eyes lifted, surprised despite herself.","\"I’ll write everything. And after that...\" His voice shook. \"Will you take me back?\"","Eira’s expression went completely flat.","\"So that’s the deal?\"","\"No. There’s no deal.\"","\"Eira—\"","\"You write it because you owe me the truth. Not because you think it buys you another chance.\"","His face crumpled.","\"Please. Is there really nothing left? Not even a little of what you felt for me?\"","Mrs. Jones gave an offended scoff.","\"The nerve of this man. He wants a second chance after spending years acting like she was disposable.\"","Eira kept her eyes on Alpha Sebastian.","\"Whatever I felt for you is gone.\"","The tears he had been holding back finally spilled over."]},{"number":192,"title":"Chapter 192 A Little Too Late","paragraphs":["Eira scratched the German shepherds behind the ears.","\"Stand down,\" she murmured. \"Good boys.\"","The guards kept hold of their leashes, forming a wall between her and Alpha Sebastian. One of them jerked his chin toward the gate.","Move.","Eira slipped her arm through Mrs. Jones’s and started toward the house.","\"Eira!\"","She glanced back.","Alpha Sebastian’s face was streaked with tears.","Then he doubled over, clutching his abdomen. Cold sweat broke across his forehead as he struggled to breathe.","One of the guards noticed.\"Ma’am?\"","Eira took one look at him.","\"Call 911. He’s in severe pain.\"","Her gaze stayed on Alpha Sebastian.","\"And I’d rather not have him die on my front walk. The Pack doesn’t need that kind of headline.\"","Then she turned to Mrs. Jones.","\"Give the dispatcher the address. Tell them he’s been bitten and is having severe abdominal pain.\"","By the time the ambulance arrived, Alpha Sebastian was barely conscious.","One of the EMTs crouched beside him.","\"How long has the pain been going on? And did the dog bite break the skin?\"","\"The handlers have the dogs’ vaccination records,\" Eira said. \"The bite is on his calf.\"","\"Is anyone riding with him?\"","\"No one from his family is here,\" Eira replied. \"He came onto private property and refused to leave.\"","Mrs. Jones folded her arms. \"Security asked him to leave more than once.\"","The EMT nodded and turned back to Alpha Sebastian.","As the ambulance pulled away from Southridge Estates, Mrs. Jones suddenly gasped.","\"Oh, shoot—the soup!\"","Mrs. Jones hurried into the house and lifted the lid from the stockpot. Steam rolled out.","\"Thank goodness,\" she said. \"It’s still simmering.\"","\"What are you making?\" Eira asked.","\"Chicken soup with vegetables and rice noodles. Nothing too heavy. You had lamb stew late this afternoon, so we’re keeping dinner light.\"","She ladled soup into a bowl and set it on the table with a small serving of steamed greens.","Eira lowered her eyes to the soup.","After a moment, she asked, \"How did you know I’ve been skipping meals?\"","\"Alpha said you have a bad habit of forgetting to eat when you get busy.\"","Eira’s spoon paused.","\"Killian?\"","Mrs. Jones’s face lit up.","\"There it is. Your boyfriend finally has a first name.\"","\"He’s not—\"","\"Mm-hmm.\"","\"He just noticed.\"","\"Of course he did.\" Mrs. Jones turned back toward the stove, smiling to herself. \"He also told me to keep extra hand cream in the bathroom. Said your hands looked sore.\"","Eira glanced down at her fingers.","The skin around her knuckles was still rough from years of neglecting herself and putting everyone else first. She had not realized Alpha Killian had noticed.","He could have seen her skip meals at work. He could have noticed the way she lost focus when she had gone too long without eating.","But he had also noticed her hands.","That small detail unsettled her more than it should have.","\"Miss Eira?\" Mrs. Jones called. \"You planning to eat that soup, or are you going to stare it into submission?\"","Eira picked up her spoon.","\"I’m eating.\"","\"That’s better.\"","Eira took a sip, then glanced toward Mrs. Jones.","\"Did he say anything else?\"","Mrs. Jones turned slowly, her eyes bright with amusement.","\"About you?\"","Eira immediately looked back at her bowl.","\"I was asking about the soup.\"","\"Sure you were.\"","Before Eira could respond, Mrs. Jones’s phone buzzed on the counter. She picked it up, typed quickly, and tried—and failed—to hide her smile.","Eira narrowed her eyes.","\"Who are you texting?\"","\"No one.\"Mrs. Jones slipped the phone into her apron pocket.","\"Eat your dinner, sweetheart.\"","--","Across town, Alpha Killian sat in the Sterling Tower boardroom, reviewing quarterly reports before the Council session.","The northern territory expansion was still under negotiation.","He preferred knowing every advantage and weakness before taking a seat at the Council table.","His phone buzzed.","Alpha Killian glanced down.","Mrs. Jones: Miss Eira just said your name.","A second message appeared.","Mrs. Jones: She also asked if you said anything else about her.","Alpha Killian’s gaze remained on the screen.","Killian: What else did she say?","Three dots appeared.","He changed his mind.","Killian: Never mind.","He didn’t need Mrs. Jones turning one quiet moment into a full-blown romance novel. Eira had said his name. That was enough.","A second later, he sent another message.","Killian: I’m hungry.","Mrs. Jones stared at the text.Then she looked over at Eira.","\"Alpha Killian says he hasn’t eaten. Would you mind if he stopped by for dinner?\"","Eira glanced at the table. He had shared her lunch and skipped dinner. He probably was hungry.\"Is there enough?\"","Mrs. Jones looked over the spread: soup, roasted chicken, vegetables, and a generous bowl of rice noodles.\"I’ll make him a plate.\"","\"I can split mine,\" Eira said. \"I haven’t touched it yet.\"","Before Mrs. Jones could object, Eira picked up her chopsticks and divided her portion in half.","Mrs. Jones watched her do it.","\"What?\"","\"Nothing.\"","\"Then quit staring.\"","Mrs. Jones hid a smile and reached for another plate.","By the time Alpha Killian arrived at Number Nine, Eira had gone upstairs to rest.","Mrs. Jones reheated his food and set the plate in front of him.\"This is the portion Miss Eira set aside for you.\"","Alpha Killian looked at the plate.\"She gave me half?\"","\"She offered.\"","That small distinction mattered more than it should have.","He thought of his parents. His mother would unwrap a square of chocolate, take one bite, and his father would immediately ask her to save him the rest.","As a kid, Alpha Killian had thought it was ridiculous.","Tonight, he sat at Eira’s table and ate the portion she had set aside for him.","It tasted better than it had any right to.","When he finished, he folded his napkin and glanced toward the stairs.","\"She asleep?\"","\"Out cold,\" Mrs. Jones said. \"She talked more tonight than I’ve heard her talk all week. Wore herself out.\"","Alpha Killian stood and headed for the door.","Then he remembered the chocolate bar in his coat pocket. Natalie had passed them around the office earlier, and he had slipped one into his pocket without thinking.","He took it out and set it on the table.","He left it whole.","For Eira.","--","The next morning, she found it beside her coffee.\"What’s this?\"","\"Alpha Killian left it.\"Mrs. Jones poured more coffee, looking far too innocent.\"He didn’t say anything. He just left it there.\"","Eira looked at the chocolate, then slipped it into her bag.","After breakfast, she texted the research center to say she would be out for the day. She had something else to take care of.","Then she opened her messages and typed Serena’s name.","Alpha Sebastian was taken to the hospital last night. Severe stomach pain.","She hit send.","If Serena still cared about Alpha Sebastian, she would show up at the hospital.","For once, Serena would have to stop hiding."]},{"number":193,"title":"Chapter 193 You Didn’t Think She’d Leave","paragraphs":["Ethan was asleep with a warm body curled against him when the hospital called.","Alpha Sebastian Hale had been admitted with severe abdominal pain.","Ethan knew Alpha Sebastian’s stomach history. Years ago, ulcers and bleeding had been routine until Eira rebuilt his life around regular meals, medication, and a strict list of foods to avoid. He had been stable for years.","So what the hell had happened?","And where was Eira?","A call like this should have gone to her first, then the Hale household, and only after that to him. If the hospital had called him directly, something in that chain had already fallen apart.","Ethan eased himself out of bed, pulled on yesterday’s jeans and a sweatshirt, and drove to Mercy General.","Alpha Sebastian was unconscious when he arrived, pale beneath the harsh hospital lights.","Ethan spent the night chasing down test results, speaking with the on-call physician, and making sure Alpha Sebastian received the medication he needed. By dawn, he had fallen asleep in the visitor’s chair beside the bed.","An hour later, a phone buzzing on the nightstand dragged him awake.","Not his phone.","Alpha Sebastian’s screen showed one name: Serena.","Ethan rubbed his eyes and answered.","\"Hey, Serena.\"","\"Ethan? You’re with Sebastian? Is he at the hospital?\"","\"Yeah. Severe abdominal pain. He’s been out since last night.\"","\"Which hospital?\"","\"Mercy General. Text me when you’re close, and I’ll come down to meet you.\"","Serena didn’t ask whether she could see Alpha Sebastian. She simply hung up.","A moment later, Alpha Sebastian stirred.","\"Ethan.\"","\"Well, look who’s back.\" Ethan reached for the water pitcher. \"What happened? You eat something that didn’t agree with you?\"","\"Water. Please.\"","Ethan filled a plastic cup and helped him sit up. Alpha Sebastian drank slowly, then sank back against the pillow.","Ethan folded his arms.","\"Your stomach’s been fine for years. What happened?\"","Alpha Sebastian stared at the ceiling.","\"I went to see Eira.\"","Ethan’s expression changed.","\"She dissolved our bond.\"","That was the piece Ethan hadn’t seen coming. He’d known their relationship was headed for a cliff, but not that Eira would take the final step so suddenly.","\"You landed in the hospital because Eira dissolved the bond?\"","\"It’s already done.\"","\"Did you sign?\"","\"She got me to sign.\"","Ethan frowned.","\"Sebastian, nobody forced you to put your name on those papers.\"","\"She got my father to push it through the Pack Council. The registry’s been updated. The bond is gone.\"","His voice cracked.","\"She lied to me for a month. She said she was staying at the Thorne estate, but she was at Southridge the whole time. She even sent someone else to the fertility classes I arranged.\"","He pressed a hand to his stomach as another cramp twisted through him.","\"A whole month, Ethan.\" His voice was thin. \"She planned all of it.\"","Ethan reached for the call button.","\"I’m fine.\"","\"You’re sweating through the sheets.\"","\"It’s not the ulcer.\"","Ethan paused, then leaned back in the chair.","Alpha Sebastian stared at the ceiling.","\"She got me to sign. She kept me out of the house, had my father push the dissolution through the Pack Council, and never said a word.\"","\"She was done talking.\"","Alpha Sebastian turned his head.","Ethan shrugged. \"What did you want her to do? Ask permission?\"","Alpha Sebastian looked away.","\"I didn’t think she’d actually leave.\"","\"No,\" Ethan said. \"You didn’t.\"","The monitor beeped steadily between them.","\"She was my mate,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","\"You knew that when you let Serena back in.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","\"That’s not fair.\"","\"I’m not trying to be fair. I’m trying to understand why you’re surprised.\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","Ethan didn’t want to push Alpha Sebastian while he was already falling apart, so he changed the subject.","\"I’ll get you some broth.\"","\"I’m not hungry,\" Alpha Sebastian murmured.His lips were pale, his eyes vacant.","Ethan sighed and left anyway. He ordered chicken soup from a nearby twenty-four-hour diner through DoorDash, then took the elevator down to the lobby to meet Serena. The driver could leave the food with the front desk.","She was already pacing near the reception desk, her heels clicking against the marble floor.","\"How does someone even get a stomach spasm?\" she demanded. \"I thought his ulcers were under control. What happened?\"","\"Stress,\" Ethan said. \"A lot of it.\"","Her pacing stopped.","\"Stress over what?\"","\"Eira dissolved the bond.\"","Serena’s eyes widened.","\"She did? And Sebastian let her?\"","\"He didn’t exactly have a choice.\"","A flicker of relief crossed her face.","\"If the bond is dissolved, then the baby is safe.\"","Ethan’s gaze dropped briefly to her stomach.","\"So that’s what you’re worried about?\"","Serena’s expression softened immediately.","\"He’s sick, Ethan. What else would I be worried about?\"","He said nothing.","She looked toward the elevators.","\"But why would Eira walk away from Sebastian? He’s an Alpha. A woman with no pack behind her doesn’t just throw away a bond like that.\"","Serena stopped herself.","Lainey’s warning came back to her—the rumors about Eira and Alpha Killian. The Sterling estate. The old bloodline. The powerful name that carried influence all the way to the Pack Council.","Serena’s mouth tightened.","The idea of Eira ending up with Alpha Killian was unbearable. She had spent months treating Eira like an outsider, only to watch her land beside one of the most powerful men in the country.","It had to be a rumor.","Alpha Killian was probably just using her.","\"Did Sebastian sign?\" Serena asked.","\"Eira got his signature. His father pushed the dissolution through the Council afterward. The registry’s already been updated.\"","Serena’s relief vanished.","\"She got him to sign?\"","\"Not exactly willingly. That’s why he’s upstairs.\"","Her eyes widened.","\"What does she have on him? Or did Alpha Killian step in and force the issue?\"","Ethan gave her a tired look.","\"I thought you wanted Sebastian free. Why do you look like someone just stole your car?\"","Serena rolled her eyes.","\"He’s in the hospital, Ethan. I’m not going to stand here and celebrate.\"","\"Right.\"","He handed her the visitor badge.","\"Go see him.\"","Serena took it, but her hand tightened around the plastic.","If Alpha Sebastian had truly lost Eira, then she needed to know exactly what he planned to do next—and whether the pup she carried still had a place in his life.","--","When Serena stepped into the hospital room, Alpha Sebastian turned his head.","He looked pale and exhausted, his face drawn beneath the fluorescent lights.","\"Why are you here?\"","The words held no warmth. No relief. Not even surprise.","Serena’s face went white, but she kept her voice gentle as she approached the bed.","\"Sebastian, how are you feeling? I came as soon as I heard you were sick.\"","\"Who told you?\"","His gaze shifted to Ethan.","Ethan immediately shook his head.","Serena frowned. She had assumed the hospital had called her, but when she opened the message, she recognized the number.","It was the same number that had texted her six weeks earlier, telling her Alpha Sebastian was drunk at a dinner party and needed someone to pick him up.","She had called back then.","No one had answered.","Since Alpha Sebastian had asked, she held out her phone.","Alpha Sebastian recognized the number instantly. He had been messaging it constantly for the past month. He knew it by heart.","\"Eira?\""]},{"number":194,"title":"Chapter 194 A Positive Test","paragraphs":["Serena’s eyes widened.","\"Eira? Six weeks ago, when you got drunk at that dinner, this was the number that told me to come get you.\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","She hadn’t cared.","Not then. Not now.","She had left him drunk in a bar, then left him doubled over in pain outside her house. Both times, she had handed him off to another woman like he was an inconvenience nobody wanted to deal with.","The realization hit hard enough to bring the pain roaring back.","His stomach clenched. His chest tightened. Cold sweat broke across his forehead.","A doctor glanced between them and checked the monitors.","\"His labs don’t show another acute bleed,\" she said carefully. \"Stress can make the spasms worse, but we’ll keep monitoring him. If the pain continues, we’ll have GI take another look.\"","She lowered her voice.","\"Once he’s stable, I’d also recommend a behavioral-health consult. Severe emotional stress can trigger very real physical symptoms.\"","Serena stood frozen beside the bed.","Losing Eira had hurt Alpha Sebastian this badly?","More than she had ever hurt him?","The thought lodged under her ribs, sharp and unwelcome.","She looked from Alpha Sebastian’s pale face to the IV dripping steadily beside him. He had barely reacted to her arrival. He had only come alive when Eira’s name entered the room.","\"I need some air,\" Serena said.","No one stopped her.","--","Down in the hospital’s women’s health building, Eira sat in a quiet alcove outside the outpatient clinics, her hair loose beneath a plain blue surgical mask.","Patients came and went around her. Some checked in at the obstetrics desk. Others crossed the atrium toward radiology, internal medicine, or the outpatient lab.","She looked like anyone else waiting for an appointment.","Only her eyes kept drifting toward the elevators.","If Serena had come to the hospital, she would almost certainly get a prenatal scan while she was there. Eira was sure of it.","Patience came easily to a scientist. So did waiting for the right result.","Sure enough, Serena appeared a few minutes later. She stepped off the elevator, spotted the Women’s Imaging sign, and slowed.","For a second, she looked as if she might turn around.","Then she squared her shoulders and walked to the registration desk.","Serena checked in and took a seat.","From across the atrium, Eira watched her fill out the paperwork.","Confirmed.","About half an hour later, a medical assistant called Serena’s name.","\"Serena Winthrop?\"","Serena stood and followed her through the doors marked Early Pregnancy Imaging.","Eira did not follow. She stayed in the public seating area, where she could see the doors without drawing attention to herself.","This early in the pregnancy, Serena was probably there for a confirmation and dating scan rather than a full prenatal workup.","At only a few weeks, the ultrasound might show little more than a gestational sac.","That was enough for Eira.","She took one discreet photo of the clinic doors as they closed behind Serena.","A few minutes later, someone emerged from the opposite corridor.","Eira recognized him immediately.","Ryan Sullivan.","They had met years ago at a research conference through Dr. Alaric Thorne.","Ryan was in his mid-forties, tall and broad-shouldered, with dark hair going silver at the temples. He had once worked as a researcher at the Silix Institute. Now he ran his own medical-technology company.","He looked as though he had just come from an appointment. A slim leather folder was tucked under one arm, and a patient checkout envelope rested on top of it.","Odd.","A man like Ryan rarely went anywhere without an assistant, a driver, or someone carrying a laptop bag behind him.","Their eyes met.","Ryan smiled and crossed the atrium.","\"Mr. Sullivan,\" Eira said.","\"Eira?\" His eyebrows lifted. \"Wow. I almost didn’t recognize you. What brings you here?\"","\"I’m waiting for someone.\"","\"Ryan,\" he said. \"You can drop the ’Mr. Sullivan.’\"","She gave him a polite smile. \"Are you all right?\"","\"Fine. Just had a follow-up and some bloodwork done.\"He glanced at his watch. \"I’ve got a meeting across town, so I should get moving.\"","\"Take care.\"","Ryan nodded and turned away.","As he passed the row of chairs, the leather folder slipped slightly under his arm. The checkout envelope slid free and landed near Eira’s feet.","Ryan didn’t notice.","Eira bent to pick it up, intending to call after him. But he had already reached the elevators.","The envelope had come partly open when it fell.","A folded lab report was sticking out just enough for Eira to catch a single line before she pushed it back inside.","Treponemal antibody screen: Reactive","RPR: Pending","Her fingers tightened around the paper.","A reactive treponemal screen did not prove an active infection. It could indicate a previous infection, successful treatment, or, less commonly, a false positive.","Before she could put the report back in the envelope, the doors to the imaging suite opened.","Serena stepped out, one hand resting protectively over her stomach.","She was alone.","Eira tucked the envelope against her thigh and moved back toward the wall.","Ryan had just reached the elevators when he glanced over his shoulder.","He saw Serena.His expression changed.","\"Serena.\"","Serena stopped.","For half a second, the color drained from her face.","Then she recovered.","\"Ryan.\"","They exchanged a look that lasted a beat too long.","Ryan glanced toward the busy atrium, then toward the emergency stairwell beside the elevators.","\"Can we talk?\"","Serena hesitated before following him through the stairwell door.","It failed to latch completely.","Eira waited until the corridor cleared, then moved closer. She stayed outside the doorway, keeping to the blind spot beside the wall.","Ryan spoke first.","\"An ultrasound?\"","His voice was low but sharp.","\"You’re pregnant?\"","Serena’s answer came after a pause.","\"It’s not yours.\"","\"Good.\" He let out a humorless laugh. \"If you were two or three months along, I might’ve wondered if the timing lined up before I went back to California.\"","Eira went still.","\"Whose is it?\" Ryan asked.","Serena ignored him.","\"What are you doing here?\"","\"That’s none of your business.\" His tone hardened. \"Did your tests come back?\"","Serena was quiet.","\"I had the ultrasound today. I’m still waiting to speak with the doctor about the bloodwork.\"","\"Right.\"","The conversation began to wind down."]},{"number":195,"title":"Chapter 195 Whose File?","paragraphs":["Eira slipped away before either of them could open the door and find her standing there.","So Ryan and Serena hadn’t merely known each other.","They had slept together.","Eira looked down at the folded report still in her hand.","The result did not prove Ryan had an active infection. It did not prove he had transmitted anything to Serena, or that Serena had transmitted anything to Alpha Sebastian.","But Ryan had slept with Serena. Serena had slept with Alpha Sebastian.","Alpha Sebastian had never slept with Eira, but they had kissed—more than once. She had never noticed a sore on his lips or inside his mouth, yet an unseen oral lesion could not be ruled out from memory alone.","The reactive treponemal screen did not prove that Ryan had an active infection, let alone prove who had infected whom.","But Eira wasn’t going to guess about her own health.","She headed for Employee Health. She needed a provider’s order, a blood draw, and actual answers.","--","Eira’s phone buzzed just as the phlebotomist inserted the needle.","Alpha Killian.","She answered.","\"Alpha Killian.\"","A quiet breath came through the line. The phlebotomist glanced up, but Eira was watching the dark red blood fill the first tube.","\"Mrs. Jones said you’re at Mercy General,\" Alpha Killian said. His voice was low, edged with tension. \"Are you there to see Alpha Sebastian?\"","\"No. I’m getting blood work.\"","\"What kind of blood work?\"","\"Someone I ran into today might have an infection, so I’m getting a full STI panel. I’m fine.\"","\"Eira—\"","The phlebotomist withdrew the needle and pressed gauze to her arm.","\"They’re wrapping me up now,\" Eira said. \"I’ll call you back.\"","\"Wait—\"","She ended the call before he could finish.","The phlebotomist taped the gauze in place.","\"Some results may come back later today. The rest could take a day or two.\"she said.","Eira nodded and held pressure over the puncture site.","Before she could stand, a woman in a white coat came down the hall. Two nurses greeted her as she passed.","\"Dr. Vale.\"","The doctor stopped in front of Eira.","\"Ms. Crawford?\"","Eira stood. \"Hi.\"","\"I’m Dr. Vale. Alpha Killian asked me to check on you.\" Her eyes flicked to the collection tubes.","\"Yes.\"","\"Come wait in my office. Alpha Killian’s on his way up.\"","Eira’s brows lifted. \"He’s coming here?\"","\"He is.\"","Dr. Vale led her down the hall, then glanced over.\"You already know my son, Barry Wood, don’t you?\"","Eira stopped.","\"Dr. Wood?\"","Dr. Vale opened her office door. \"Vale’s my maiden name. I kept it for work. Barry took his dad’s last name.\"","\"Barry lives across town with his grandmother. His father and I still work brutal hours, so we don’t see him as much as we’d like.\"","At the mention of Mrs. Wood, Eira relaxed and followed her inside.","\"I’ve been out there twice,\" she said. \"Mrs. Wood and Barry were both really kind to me.\"","\"So I heard.\" Dr. Vale smiled. \"And that herbal hair rinse you use—that’s her recipe, isn’t it?\"","\"It is.\"","\"My hair’s still dark because of that woman.\" Dr. Vale nodded toward Eira’s arm. \"You can toss the gauze now.\"","Eira dropped it into the trash and pulled her sleeve over the bandage.","\"I’ve got rounds,\" Dr. Vale said, gathering a folder from her desk. \"Wait here for Alpha Killian. I flagged your order as urgent, so we should have some results this afternoon.\"","She paused at the door.","\"You know who owns Mercy General, right?\"","Eira’s eyes narrowed. \"The Sterlings.\"","\"Bingo.\"","Dr. Vale left, closing the door behind her.","Eira immediately called Mrs. Jones.","\"The hospital Sebastian was brought to—Mercy General. It’s a Sterling facility.\"","\"It is,\" Mrs. Jones said, unbothered. \"If the Hales try anything, we’ll hear about it first.\"","The conversation drifted to dinner after that—until a knock at the door cut it short.","\"I’ll call you back,\" Eira said.","She ended the call and opened the door.","Alpha Killian stood in the hallway, broad-shouldered and sharply dressed, the cold still clinging to his dark coat.","He filled the doorway.","His gaze dropped straight to the bandage on her arm.","\"What happened?\"","He was already asking questions before he finished stepping inside.","\"What made you run an STI panel?\"","Eira told him about the stairwell and handed him the folded report.","His expression tightened as he scanned the page.","\"Serena and Ryan Sullivan?\"","\"They have history. She said it happened before he moved back to California.\"","Alpha Killian knew Sullivan’s background. His company was small, but its remote patient-monitoring platform turned a real profit, and word was he’d been hiring aggressively for a new diagnostics project.","\"They probably crossed paths at work.\"Alpha Killian said.","His eyes dropped to the report again. His jaw tightened.","Then he folded the page and slid it back across the desk.","\"Your results should be back this afternoon. We’ll wait.\"","\"We?\"","Alpha Killian pulled out a chair. \"I can sit still when it matters.\"","Despite herself, Eira almost smiled.","She sat across from him.","The wait was quiet. Eira wasn’t worried. She had never slept with Alpha Sebastian, and since Serena resurfaced, she could count the times they’d even been in the same room on one hand.","Alpha Killian, though, was already running the scenarios.","If the panel came back clean, they’d move on.","If it didn’t, he’d handle it.","By late afternoon, Dr. Vale returned with the report.","\"Everything’s negative,\" she said. \"The treponemal screen and the RPR are both nonreactive, and the rest of the panel is clear.\"","Eira’s shoulders eased.","Across from her, Alpha Killian’s fingers slowly unclenched.","She was fine.","That was all that mattered.","After Dr. Vale left, Eira folded the report and tucked it into her bag.","\"Mercy General takes patient privacy pretty seriously, doesn’t it?\"","Alpha Killian looked at her.","\"Very seriously.\"","He caught the real question underneath it before she said another word.","\"Whose file do you want?\""]},{"number":196,"title":"Chapter 196 Rotten Logic","paragraphs":["\"Serena just came out of the OB-GYN clinic,\" Eira said. \"She had another ultrasound.\"","Alpha Killian understood exactly what she was implying.","\"I’ll handle it.\"","He almost told her that he would handle anything that worried her. He would take care of every detail, solve every problem, and ask for nothing in return.","Eira looked into his dark eyes, and something warm stirred in her chest.","He had said it so easily. No questions. No conditions. Just three simple words that made her feel, for one brief second, as if she did not have to deal with everything alone.","Her heartbeat quickened.","She looked away before he could notice.","\"I’m putting all my time into the research institute’s partnership with Sterling Group,\" she said. \"Everything else can wait.\"","Alpha Killian stared at her.","She really did not understand what he was offering, did she?","Eira felt his eyes on her and grew even more uncomfortable. She needed to change the subject.","\"And thank you for finding Dr. Vale and getting my results rushed.\"","His brow lifted slightly.","At least she had remembered him.","Then he noticed how pale she looked.","That was not right. Mrs. Jones fed her like royalty.","\"You haven’t eaten?\"","\"I had breakfast.\" Eira looked down at herself, confused. \"Why?\"","\"You look pale.\"","He suspected her blood sugar had dropped. He reached for his phone, ready to ask Kate Morgan to bring her something sweet.","Before he could make the call, Eira pulled a small chocolate bar from her coat pocket.","The same one he had left at Number Nine the night before.","\"Maybe my blood sugar is low,\" she said.","She peeled back the wrapper and took a small bite.","Alpha Killian put his phone away and watched her eat. She took small, careful bites, completely focused on the chocolate. She ate the same way she handled everything else, quietly and with care.","When Eira caught him staring, she removed the rest of the wrapper and broke the bar in half. Then she held out the untouched piece to him.","A soft sound left her throat.\"Here. Have some.\"","Alpha Killian stared at the chocolate in her hand.","He never ate the stuff. It stuck to his teeth, and afterward it made his mouth look like he had been chewing tar.","But Eira was sharing it with him.","He took the piece and bit off a small corner.","When she saw him eat it, the corners of her eyes and mouth lifted into a faint, pleased smile.","\"Eira?\"","The voice came from behind them.","Eira turned.","Ethan Yates was walking toward them. He slowed as soon as he saw her, as if he needed a second to make sure he was looking at the right person.","He had seen the news articles about Dr. Crawford, but he had never connected that brilliant, confident woman with the quiet Eira he remembered.","The difference was not in her face.","It was in the way she carried herself.","Her clothes were simple, expensive, and perfectly tailored. Her hair fell in glossy waves, and her skin looked healthy beneath the hospital lights. Even beside Alpha Killian, whose Alpha presence filled the hallway, she did not look small or dependent.","She stood on her own.","No wonder Alpha Sebastian could not let her go. No wonder he had ended up in the hospital with stomach spasms after receiving the divorce papers. Anyone would hate losing a woman like Eira.","Ethan stopped several feet away.","With Alpha Killian beside her, he knew better than to step into their space. Alpha Killian’s scent had sharpened, carrying a quiet warning that every wolf nearby would have understood.","Watch yourself.","\"Eira, are you here to see Sebastian?\"","\"He didn’t tell you we’re divorced?\" Eira asked.","Ethan blinked. \"I only just found out.\"","Eira had always known Ethan was good at playing dumb and talking his way out of trouble.","\"Mr. Yates, you knew Serena was Sebastian’s ex, didn’t you? You also knew they were still involved after the wedding. You knew long before I did, didn’t you?\"","The color drained from Ethan’s face.","Before he could answer, Alpha Killian looked at him.","The air seemed to tighten.","Ethan felt the weight of the Alpha’s attention settle over him. It was not a direct command, but every wolf in the hallway understood the message.","Watch yourself.","Ethan swallowed and turned back to Eira.","\"Sebastian was wrong. I know that. You don’t have to forgive him. But could you at least go see him? He hasn’t eaten all day. He’s getting weaker, and his stomach was already in bad shape. Not eating will only make it worse.\"","Eira did not move.","\"How is that my problem?\"","It was not really a question. Her voice was flat.","Even Ethan felt a chill. He had expected anger. He had not expected her to sound this calm.","\"You spent all that time getting his stomach under control,\" he said. \"Now it’s acting up again. Doesn’t that make everything you did for him pointless?\"","Eira stared at him.","She could not believe he was actually making that argument.","Alpha Killian’s voice turned cold.","\"She helped him recover. She didn’t leave with his stomach tucked under her arm. That was already more mercy than he deserved.\"","Ethan flinched.","He did not dare argue with Alpha Killian. The dominant pressure coming off him filled the hallway, and Ethan’s wolf urged him to lower his eyes.","But Alpha Sebastian was still his best friend.","\"Alpha Killian, that’s not exactly fair.\"","\"Isn’t it?\" Alpha Killian asked.","He was still looking at Eira, not Ethan.","\"No,\" Eira said. \"The logic is perfectly sound.\"","Ethan stared at her.","Eira turned toward him and explained it in the same calm tone she might have used in a business meeting.","\"Sebastian worked himself sick trying to make money for Serena’s career. That is how he damaged his stomach. I put in the time and effort to help him recover. Then I found out what kind of hypocrite he was, so I left.\"","She paused.","\"By your logic, the stomach I repaired should have packed its bags and left with me.\"","Ethan nearly choked.","Apparently, that was one way to look at it.","Eira watched his stunned expression.","\"So if his stomach is acting up again, that makes perfect sense.\"","Alpha Killian gave a slow nod.","\"Too bad you couldn’t take it with you.\"","Eira turned to him. \"That would be a felony, Killian.\"","\"Good to know.\"","Ethan stared at them.","They had completely shut him out of the conversation. Worse, they seemed to understand each other without trying. Every time he tried to push Eira toward Alpha Sebastian, Alpha Killian stepped in and turned the argument back on him.","There was no winning against both of them.","\"Eira, do you really have to be this harsh?\" Ethan asked. \"You and Sebastian were married.\"","\"We were married. That is exactly why I will not let this slide.\"","Her tone stayed polite, which somehow made the words cut deeper.","\"Do me a favor and give Sebastian a message,\" she continued. \"In the lawsuit over the marital assets, I’m not naming Serena alone. I’m naming Sebastian as a defendant too.\"","Ethan’s expression tightened.","\"You’re suing both of them?\"","\"I’m holding both of them accountable.\"","Alpha Killian’s gaze shifted to Ethan. The warning in his eyes was unmistakable.","Ethan took a step back.","Eira adjusted the strap of her bag and met his eyes.","\"Make sure Sebastian understands. This isn’t a bluff, and it isn’t something I’ll get over by tomorrow.\""]},{"number":197,"title":"Chapter 197 One Last Chance","paragraphs":["Ethan had not seen the asset claim coming.","As Eira and Alpha Killian disappeared down the hall, he finally connected the dots. Alpha Sebastian had poured joint assets into Serena’s career after registering his mate bond with Eira.","Under Pack law, Eira could demand a full accounting and recover her share.","The case could ruin Alpha Sebastian.","Ethan returned to the room but kept quiet. Eira still needed bank records and proof.","\"How’re you feeling?\" he asked. \"The doctor wants you here overnight. If your labs are clear tomorrow, you can go home.\"","Alpha Sebastian was already yanking off the monitor leads.","\"What the hell are you doing?\"","\"Going after Eira.\"","\"You can barely stand.\"","\"She left me.\"","His voice cracked. His face was white, and his hands shook as he reached for his shirt.","Ethan blocked the door. \"Seb, chasing her through a hospital won’t fix this.\"","\"It’s not over.\"","\"You’re already divorced.\"","\"She hasn’t chosen another mate.\"","Ethan stared at him. \"This isn’t a bad deal you can renegotiate. You hurt her.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw locked. \"Move.\"","The door opened before Ethan could answer.","Alpha Carter walked in with Finn.","Alpha Sebastian froze. \"Alpha Carter. Finn.\"","Alpha Carter glanced at Alpha Sebastian’s hospital bracelet and half-buttoned shirt.","\"Going somewhere?\" he asked. \"Because Mercy General already has doctors. They don’t need you making rounds.\"","\"We heard you were sick,\" Finn added. \"Dad wanted to check in.\"","Alpha Carter’s sharp gaze said this was not a social call.","As Hale Group’s largest outside investor, Alpha Carter had enough shares to sway the board. Alpha Sebastian could not blow him off to chase a personal crisis, especially when the company and the Hale Pack were already under pressure.","His jaw clenched, but he returned to the bed.","Ethan stepped aside. \"I’ll give you some privacy.\"","As he passed Alpha Sebastian, he lowered his voice.","\"Don’t go after her tonight. You’ll only make it worse.\"","Then he left and closed the door.","Alpha Carter’s eyes moved around the room before settling on the untouched bowl of oatmeal cooling on the tray.","\"Your stomach is acting up, and you still aren’t eating?\" he said. \"That is not going to help.\"","He sat down.","\"I appreciate your concern, Alpha Carter. I just don’t have much of an appetite.\"","Alpha Sebastian lowered himself into the chair across from him.","He already knew Alpha Carter had heard everything. The divorce. The failed patent deal with Dr. Shaw. A visit at this hour meant the friendly conversation would not last long.","Alpha Carter was starting with the polite version.","\"A man can’t run on an empty tank,\" Alpha Carter said. \"The doctor has you on soft foods, I assume?\"","\"Yes, Alpha Carter.\"","\"Finn.\" Alpha Carter glanced at his son. \"Have someone send over some broth. Something light.\"","\"Got it.\"","Finn pulled out his phone.","\"Please, don’t go to the trouble,\" Alpha Sebastian said quickly. His voice was still weak. \"Your coming here is already more than I deserve.\"","Alpha Carter waved him off.","\"I’ve watched what you built at Hale Group. The deals you closed, the numbers you brought in, the growth. I’ve kept all of it in mind.\"","[Here it comes,] Alpha Sebastian thought.","He held his breath.","The bill had come due.","\"After the last mess, I did what I could to keep it quiet,\" Alpha Carter continued. \"But you can’t keep a wildfire under control forever, especially when you keep throwing sparks into the flames.\"","Alpha Carter’s frown deepened.","\"When I backed you, you should have understood how many people were watching you.\"","He paused.","\"They were watching me too.\"","For a man in Alpha Carter’s position, one bad decision could cost him more than a business deal. It could cost him his seat at the table.","As one of Hale Group’s largest shareholders and a senior voice in Pack politics, Alpha Carter understood both systems.","The board cared about stock value, contracts, and legal exposure. The Pack Council cared about territory, resources, and whether an Alpha could still protect his people.","If Alpha Sebastian lost the board, he could lose the company. If he lost the Council, he could lose Hale territory.","And right now, both sides were closing in.","Alpha Sebastian had brought this on himself. He had kept Eira out of the boardroom because she did not fit the image he wanted for the Hale Pack. She dressed simply, stayed out of the spotlight, and had no powerful family name behind her. He had refused to acknowledge her as his mate because he thought she made him look ordinary.","He had been wrong.","Eira had managed his household, handled Pack affairs, and helped secure the Snowmark partnership.","While Alpha Sebastian chased status, she kept the Hale Pack running. Her work had helped fund border patrols, security teams, and emergency housing for displaced Omegas.","He had used her when it suited him, then treated her like a liability.","Now the whole mess was coming back to bite him.","\"I understand, Alpha Carter.\" Alpha Sebastian lowered his eyes. \"My parents pushed the dissolution through. I never approved it. And Dr. Shaw only agreed to work with me because Eira introduced us. After she left, he had no reason to stay in business with me.\"","His throat tightened.","\"I misjudged her. I didn’t know what I had until I lost it. That was on me.\"","He paused, then added, \"Whatever the board decides, I’ll accept it.\"","\"The board isn’t going to sweep this under the rug,\" Alpha Carter said sharply. \"If the affair, the divorce, and the failed deals become public, the damage won’t stop with you. It will hit Hale Group, Carter Group, and every investor tied to us.\"","He rested one hand on the edge of the desk.","\"That division pays for our expansion, our security teams, and the Pack’s border patrols. If we lose it, we lose revenue, credibility, and the resources that keep this territory secure.\"","Alpha Sebastian stayed silent.","He knew Alpha Carter was right. A failing Alpha did not just lose money. He lost trust. Once Pack members began to doubt his ability to protect their homes and families, rival Alphas would test the borders.","Alpha Carter’s expression hardened before his tone suddenly eased.","\"The board voted to keep you in place, but only under strict conditions.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked up.","\"Keep the Snowmark partnership,\" Alpha Carter said. \"And make sure Eira keeps the divorce private. Do both, and you may still have a way out.\"","There was no relief in Alpha Sebastian’s chest.","Alpha Carter stood and buttoned his coat.","\"As for Eira, I told you years ago that you sometimes have to let go to get what you want. If you can’t stay away from her, send her somewhere far from the Pack’s spotlight.\"","He gave Alpha Sebastian one last look.","\"When the timing is right, you can always try to win her back. Just keep the mess quiet until then.\""]},{"number":198,"title":"Chapter 198 The Money Trail","paragraphs":["\"Thanks for the heads-up, Alpha Carter.\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice sounded raw.","Alpha Carter held his gaze. \"Listen to me. This is the last time I stick my neck out for you. Screw up again, and you’re on your own. I carry weight with the board and the Pack Council, but I’m not spending that capital on an Alpha who can’t keep his company steady or his territory secure.\"","The last trace of color drained from Alpha Sebastian’s face. \"Understood.\"","\"Good. Get some sleep. Tomorrow’s going to be brutal.\"","Alpha Sebastian started to stand, but Alpha Carter waved him back.","\"Don’t get up. You look like hell.\" He glanced around the private room. \"Where’s Jordan?\"","\"Putting out a fire on the Snowmark account.\"","Alpha Carter gave a curt nod.","Finn tucked his phone into his bomber jacket. \"I had someone pick up chicken noodle soup from that place you like. It should all be here within the hour.\"","\"Thanks,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","Alpha Carter and Finn stepped into the hall. The moment the door closed, Finn turned to his father.","\"I thought the plan was to keep him on a short leash. Why tell him exactly how much influence we have over the board?\"","Alpha Carter gave him a thin smile. \"Because a threat works better when the man knows it has teeth.\"","\"And if he screws up again?\"","\"I’ll push the board to pull him out of day-to-day operations and put you in charge of the division.\"","Finn frowned. \"All this because he can’t let Eira go?\"","\"Eira isn’t the problem. His judgment is.\"","\"She’s not his mate anymore,\" Finn said.","Alpha Carter stopped and studied him. Out of everything they had discussed, that was the detail his son had chosen to correct.","\"Fiona says you’re into her.\"","Finn’s jaw tightened. \"Fiona needs to stay out of my business.\"","\"There’s nothing wrong with wanting a good woman.\"","\"Eira isn’t a deal to close.\"","\"No,\" Alpha Carter agreed. \"She’s smart, loyal, and better connected than Sebastian ever bothered to find out. Any Pack would be lucky to have someone like her as Luna.\"","Finn’s expression cooled. \"If you’re about to tell me to claim her for the family, don’t. She just walked away from a marriage where everyone treated her like an asset. I’m not doing the same thing.\"","Alpha Carter went quiet for a beat. Then one corner of his mouth lifted.","\"Good. At least one of you gets it.\"","He resumed walking.","\"If you’re serious about her, don’t chase her like disputed territory. Give her space. Earn her trust. And let her decide what happens next.\"","--","On the top floor of Silix’s R&D center, Claire dropped into a conference chair and looked from Professor Davies to Eira.","\"We’re the client here, right? I thought being in-house was supposed to be the cushy side of tech.\"","Davies let out a dry laugh. \"Cushy? You have weekends, normal hours, and time to eat lunch somewhere other than your desk. When we were building the Sovereign processor, half the team kept toothbrushes in the lab. If the verification data came back wrong at midnight, nobody went home.\"","Claire winced. \"Okay. Point taken.\"","Eira set a bottle of sparkling water in front of her.","\"You and Professor Davies stay focused on the core work,\" Claire said. \"Architecture, algorithms, verification, and IP. That’s the heart of the project. I’ll deal with budgets, vendors, and everyone who thinks marking an email urgent makes it important.\"","Davies chuckled. \"Now you’re learning.\"","Then he turned to Eira. \"Have you made a decision about Stanford? They’re waiting on your answer to the faculty offer.\"","\"It can wait.\" Eira closed the report on her tablet. \"Sovereign comes first. I gave Killian my word.\"","Claire’s head came up. She rolled her pen between her fingers.","\"Killian now? You and Mr.Sterling sound pretty close.\"","\"He’s my business partner.\"","\"Just a business partner?\"","Eira paused. \"He’s Lila’s brother. We’re friends.\"","\"Right.\" Claire nodded with a smile that said she believed none of it. \"Friends.\"","Davies spared Eira from answering.","\"If you’re going all in on Sovereign, I assume you’re turning down other projects. Remember Ryan Sullivan? He wanted to talk to you.\"","Eira’s hand stilled on her tablet.","\"What does he want?\"","\"A consulting agreement. He knows your schedule is packed, so he asked me to feel you out before he contacted you directly.\"","Ryan was an old friend of Dr. Alaric Thorne’s. Out of respect for him, Eira wasn’t ready to turn the offer down outright.","\"Sovereign needs my full attention. I can’t take on another chip project and pretend I can do both well.\"","\"That’s what I told him.\" Davies leaned back. \"I’ll pass along the answer. Don’t give it another thought.\"","Eira hesitated. \"You haven’t met with Sullivan recently, have you? Dinner, drinks, anything like that?\"","Davies raised an eyebrow. \"No. I’ve barely had time to grab takeout, let alone sit through dinner with him.\"","The chance of casual contact causing any problem was almost nonexistent. Eira knew that. Still, some of the tension left her shoulders.","\"He’ll find another consultant,\" Davies added. \"Someone will take the check.\"","Serena’s face flashed through Eira’s mind. She and Sullivan moved in the same social circle. If Eira passed, Serena might see an opening.","A knock cut through the room.","Alpha Killian stepped inside in a charcoal suit, the collar of his white shirt open at the throat. He greeted Davies and Claire with a brief nod before his silver-gray eyes settled on Eira.","\"Do you have a minute?\"","Eira slid her tablet toward Davies. \"The latest design files are in the secure folder. Pay close attention to the thermal results on the third architecture. I’ll be right back.\"","She followed Alpha Killian into the hall.","\"What happened?\"","\"My office.\"","The glass skybridge connected the R&D center to Sterling Tower. Below them, rush-hour traffic crawled through Palo Alto while lights flickered on across the Sterling campus.","Pack guards secured the perimeter and underground garage. Inside the research buildings, Sterling’s private security team monitored every badge and visitor.","Alpha Killian walked beside Eira in silence. He could have called her office or sent someone. Instead, he had crossed the bridge to get her himself.","It was a small thing, but Eira noticed.","When they reached the executive floor, Kate and Natalie were packing up for the evening. Both women stopped when they saw Eira.","\"Miles is back,\" Natalie said, handing her a small paper bag. \"He brought us all souvenirs. You got the good stuff.\"","Kate held up a box of matcha cookies. \"I got snacks. You clearly outrank me.\"","Eira smiled. \"I’ll trade.\"","\"Not a chance.\" Kate tucked the box against her side. \"Miles is waiting in Killian’s office. Susan’s in there too.\"","The smile faded from Eira’s face.","Susan was her attorney. If she and Miles were both waiting, this had nothing to do with Sterling business.","Eira looked at Alpha Killian.","His expression remained unreadable, but his voice softened.","\"Miles finished tracing Alpha Sebastian’s payments to Serena.\"","\"And?\"","\"Not one dollar went into research.\""]},{"number":199,"title":"Chapter 199 The Brain Trust","paragraphs":["Miles and Susan were waiting in the seating area when Eira and Alpha Killian walked in. Susan closed her laptop, while Miles set his coffee aside and got straight to business.","He slid a tablet across the low table. \"Ms. Crawford, this is everything we found overseas. Bank records, leases, hotel receipts, event photos. It’s all dated, sourced, and cross-referenced.\"","He opened a manila folder and spread several photographs across the table.","\"Serena kept a low profile for her first six months in Europe,\" Miles said. \"Then Alpha Sebastian’s money started coming in.\"","Eira picked up a photo. Serena stood under a crystal chandelier with a champagne flute in one hand, surrounded by men in tuxedos. A designer gown hugged her figure, and diamonds glittered at her throat.","\"After that, she upgraded fast,\" Miles continued. \"Luxury rentals, five-star hotels, designer clothes, private events, and restaurants with month-long waitlists. She spent more time networking at fundraisers and launch parties than she did in a lab.\"","He tapped the financial summary on the screen.","\"Alpha Sebastian wired her money for more than three years. \"","Susan leaned forward. \"Do we have enough to trace the money back to marital assets?\"","\"Yes. The transfers came from accounts opened after Eira and Alpha Sebastian registered their mate bond. We also found payments routed through Hale Group, but I flagged those separately. Outside counsel will need to determine whether they were authorized business expenses.\"","Eira turned to the next photograph and went still.","Ryan Sullivan stood beside Serena with one hand resting low on her waist. Unlike the other men in the pictures, he wasn’t looking at the camera. He was looking at Serena.","So this was how they had met.","Ryan had money, influence, and connections Serena could use.","Apparently, she did have a type.","Useful men.","Alpha Killian glanced at the photograph in Eira’s hand. His silver-gray eyes narrowed.","\"Something you recognize?\"","Eira set the photograph down, holding back a smile. \"I’d pay good money to see Sebastian’s face when he gets this.\"","She paused.","\"Vincent’s too.\"","Alpha Sebastian had always been Serena’s biggest supporter. Vincent had defended her almost as fiercely. Neither man would enjoy learning that Serena had a history with Ryan Sullivan they knew nothing about.","Alpha Killian pictured their reactions, and the corner of his mouth lifted.","Susan pulled the tablet closer. \"Here’s the rough breakdown. Alpha Sebastian transferred more than one hundred million dollars over three years. About thirty million can be tied to real research. At least sixty million paid for Serena’s apartment, travel, cars, clothes, and social life. We’re still tracing the rest.\"","\"He called it a private investment,\" Eira said.","\"He can call it whatever he wants,\" Susan replied. \"There are no shares, repayment terms, progress reports, or research results. Most of the money went straight to Serena’s personal expenses. We’ll argue that Alpha Sebastian disguised unauthorized gifts as business investments.\"","\"How much can we recover?\"","\"You can demand a full accounting and seek reimbursement for your share of the community property. Pack law gives us another claim because Alpha Sebastian transferred bonded assets without your consent.\" Susan tapped the screen. \"I can’t promise we’ll recover every dollar. That depends on the records and whether Serena knew where the money came from.\"","\"The pregnancy may keep Alpha Sebastian paying her bills,\" Alpha Killian said.","\"Then we keep tracing the payments,\" Susan replied. \"If the timeline becomes important, we’ll request the necessary records through the court.\"","Eira nodded. \"What’s next?\"","\"We preserve the evidence, send a demand letter, and give them a deadline to respond. If they ignore it, we file.\"","\"No settlement,\" Eira said.","Susan met her eyes. \"Understood. The letter gives them notice. It doesn’t mean you have to negotiate.\"","She closed the file.","\"Serena spent years living large on money that came out of your marriage. We don’t have to make this easy for her.\"","Eira looked at the photograph again.","Serena had taken enough shots at her.","It was time to return one.","\"Send the letters,\" Eira said.","\"How long do we give them?\" Susan asked. \"Fifteen days is standard. Ten is aggressive but fair.\"","\"Three,\" Alpha Killian said.","Susan shook her head. \"For a nine-figure claim? Their attorneys would call it a stunt.\"","\"Ten, then,\" Eira said.","\"Ten days to respond and provide an initial accounting,\" Susan clarified. \"If they refuse, we file. If they start moving assets, we go to court sooner.\"","\"Can we keep this quiet until the letters arrive?\" Eira asked.","\"We can control our side. No leaks and no calls.\"","Alpha Killian looked at Susan. \"Send Serena’s letter to the Winthrop estate and her last known address. Send Alpha Sebastian’s to his home and copy his attorney.\"","\"If Hale accounts were involved, the company gets a separate preservation notice,\" Susan said. \"I’ll use certified mail, overnight delivery, and email to authorized counsel. Their response is due at five p.m. Pacific, ten days from tomorrow.\"","\"No room to play dumb,\" Miles said.","\"Exactly.\"","Susan closed the file.","The letters would not freeze the money or guarantee a win. They would force Alpha Sebastian and Serena to respond while Susan prepared to file.","If they moved the assets, she would go to court.","If they stayed silent, she would sue.","Simple. Clean. It reminded Eira of a Sterling border patrol closing in on rogues who had crossed too deep into Pack territory. No wasted motion. No open route of escape."]},{"number":200,"title":"Chapter 200 Out of Her League","paragraphs":["It was well past dinner, and they were still buried in financial records, demand letters, and filing plans. Eira finally closed her notebook.","\"That’s enough for tonight. When did any of you last eat?\"","Miles glanced at his empty coffee cup. \"Do airport pretzels count?\"","\"No,\" Susan and Eira said at the same time.","Alpha Killian leaned back in his chair. \"Let’s get dinner.\"","\"Any allergies or foods you hate?\" Eira asked.","\"I’m easy,\" Susan said.","\"Same,\" Miles added. \"As long as it’s hot.\"","Eira called the farm-to-table restaurant where they had celebrated Dr. Shaw’s birthday. The kitchen was closing soon, but the host agreed to hold a quiet table upstairs.","\"You know my order,\" Alpha Killian said as she hung up.","Eira glanced at him. \"Lila gave me your entire food profile.\"","\"Of course she did.\"","Twenty minutes later, Eira climbed into Alpha Killian’s SUV. Miles took one look at the front passenger seat, then headed for Susan’s car.","\"I’ll ride with counsel,\" he said.","Susan raised an eyebrow. \"How thoughtful.\"","\"I have excellent survival instincts.\"","Halfway to the restaurant, Lila called.","\"Eira! Professor Chase finally approved my paper.\"","Eira smiled at the excitement in her voice. \"That’s great. Have you eaten?\"","\"Does iced coffee count?\"","\"No. Come have dinner with us.\" Eira texted her the address. \"You know everyone.\"","\"Perfect. I’m starving.\"","Lila pulled into the parking lot fifteen minutes later in a dark green vintage Mustang. She stepped out in jeans, ankle boots, and a cropped leather jacket, looking very pleased with herself.","Alpha Killian stared at the car. \"Since when do you drive a Mustang?\"","\"Since I got taste.\" Lila linked her arm through Eira’s. \"Team Eira has standards.\"","Alpha Killian looked from his sister to the car, trying to figure out what one had to do with the other.","Before he could ask, Lila pulled Eira toward the entrance.","\"Don’t tell him where I got the car,\" she whispered. \"He’ll take the keys and call it a safety inspection.\"","Eira glanced back. \"Would he really?\"","\"He’s a control freak with an Alpha complex. What do you think?\" Lila leaned closer. \"Besides, I need every advantage I can get.\"","\"Against whom?\"","\"My brother, obviously. I plan to stay your favorite Sterling.\"","Eira laughed. \"You’re still number one.\"","\"For real?\"","\"For real.\"","Lila hugged her, grinning over Eira’s shoulder at Alpha Killian.","A few steps behind them, Alpha Killian’s face went cold.","Susan glanced at Miles. \"Should we warn her?\"","\"Not a chance,\" Miles said. \"I like my job.\"","Their private dining room was on the second floor. As they reached the landing, the door across the hall opened.","Finn and Fiona Carter stepped out first. Vincent followed with Lainey and Logan Harris.","Eira slowed.","Fiona had not expected to spend the evening with the Crawfords. She and Vincent were hardly friends. The last time they had spoken, she had torn into him for defending Serena.","But Lainey had recently signed on as an ambassador for one of Carter Group’s fashion brands, which meant she and Fiona would be working together.","Vincent was also flying back to D.C. soon and wanted someone reliable to keep an eye on Lainey while he was gone.","When Vincent invited Fiona to dinner, Alpha Carter advised her to accept. Refusing a Crawford invitation would only create more Pack gossip.","Fiona had agreed, then brought Finn along so she would not have to face the awkward dinner alone.","Now both groups stood frozen on the landing.","\"Alpha Killian. Eira.\" Fiona recovered first and greeted them with an easy smile.","Finn lit up the moment he saw Eira. \"You’re having dinner here too? At this hour?\" He glanced at Alpha Killian. \"Please tell me Sterling isn’t making you work all night.\"","His concern was so open that Eira almost laughed.","\"We just wrapped up,\" she said. \"And it was personal business, not work.\"","That took the fight right out of him. \"Oh. Okay, then.\"","Eira noticed Lainey watching her. It was not the usual look of a photographer studying someone’s face. This was quieter. Almost unsettled.","Lainey gave her a small smile. \"We keep running into each other.\"","\"Looks that way,\" Eira replied with a polite nod.","Lila greeted the others, then linked her arm through Eira’s. \"Come on. I’m starving.\"","She pulled Eira into their private room. Alpha Killian followed without looking at anyone, including Lainey.","Vincent’s jaw tightened. His sister had tried to catch Alpha Killian’s attention, and the man had walked past her as if she were part of the wallpaper.","After the door closed, Fiona frowned.","\"Finn, was that Susan?\"","Vincent knew the name. Susan was one of California’s top family-law attorneys. In Pack circles, she was famous for handling ugly mate-bond dissolutions and multimillion-dollar asset fights.","Vincent stared at the closed door.","Lainey caught the look on his face. \"What?\"","\"Eira and Alpha Sebastian already dissolved their bond,\" he said. \"Why would she still need a divorce attorney?\"","He turned to Fiona. \"Have you heard anything?\"","\"No.\" Fiona pulled out her phone, but an uneasy thought had already hit her. If Eira planned to go after Alpha Sebastian over hidden marital assets, the fallout could reach Carter Group, Hale Group’s largest outside shareholder.","\"I need to make a call.\" She slipped her phone into her clutch and looked at the others. \"Thanks for dinner. Let’s do this again when nobody has a flight to catch.\"","Then she grabbed Finn’s sleeve and headed for the stairs.","Finn looked back at Eira’s door. \"You know I can walk by myself, right?\"","\"Then walk faster.\"","Vincent, Lainey, and Logan left soon after. In the back of the black SUV, Logan loosened his tie and glanced at Vincent.","\"Relax. I’ll check in on Lainey while you’re in D.C. If she needs anything, she calls me first.\"","\"I know,\" Vincent said.","Lainey barely heard them. She could not stop thinking about Eira’s face. The eyes were different, but the shape of her cheekbones and the line of her jaw looked strangely familiar.","She looked like Henry Crawford.","Lainey wanted to ask whether Vincent had noticed. Before she could, he mistook her silence for something else.","\"Let Alpha Killian go,\" he said. \"You know he and Eira are seeing each other.\"","Logan turned sharply from the front passenger seat. \"Hold on. Alpha Killian Sterling and Eira? Since when?\"","If that news hit the Pack grapevine, every well-connected family on the East Coast would be talking by breakfast. Alpha Killian belonged to one of the country’s oldest Alpha bloodlines. For years, powerful Packs had treated him like the most valuable unmated Alpha in North America.","Lainey ignored Logan and looked at her brother.","\"What do you really think of Eira?\"","Vincent did not hesitate. \"She’s out of her depth.\"","Lainey went still.","Vincent assumed she was comparing herself to Eira.","\"Look, I’m not crazy about you chasing Alpha Killian,\" he continued. \"But Eira isn’t someone you need to worry about. If he chooses her, that’s his call and his mistake. You’re a Crawford. She has no family, no Pack, and no connections worth mentioning.\"","Lainey tightened her grip on her purse.","\"No family?\"","\"She grew up in an Omega group home. \"","Lainey’s heart slammed against her ribs.","For one dizzy second, she forgot how to breathe."]}]);
